hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"8401","Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from Abu Hurayrah. 8396 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took - I think he said: My hand - from the market of Banu Qaynuqa', neither speaking to me nor I speaking to him, until he stood at the door of Fatimah and said: Is the little boy there? - meaning al-Hasan. Abu Hurayrah said: I thought his mother kept him back to wash his face and dress him - I think he said: A necklace - then he came out to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who embraced him and said: O Allah, love him and love whoever loves him."
"8402","8397 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Abi al-Hunayn narrated to us, he said: Abu Ghassan narrated to us, he said: Warqa' narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), something similar to it."
"8403","8398 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj who said: Umar ibn Ata' informed me, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of the imam is better than twenty-five prayers he prays alone. We do not know that Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid narrated from Nafi' ibn Jubayr except the first hadith, nor that Umar ibn Ata' narrated from Nafi', from Abu Hurayrah, except: The prayer of the imam is better."
"8404","8399 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us - as I think - he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from al-Qasim - I think - from Ibn Abbas; and some who narrated it from Ibn Abi Dhi'b said: From al-Qasim ibn Mihran, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: People follow Quraysh in this matter; their best follow their best, and their worst follow their worst."
"8405","8400 - Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Khallad al-Bahili narrated to us, he said: Ma'n ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: A caller calls every night when what Allah wills of the night has passed: Who supplicates to Me so I may answer him? Who asks Me so I may give him? Or words similar to this speech, resembling this meaning."
"8406","8401 - al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub al-Rukhami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud al-Jazari narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from al-Qasim, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dream of a believer is one part of forty-six parts of prophethood."
"8407","Ata, freedman of Abu Ahmad, from Abu Hurayrah. 8402 - Ahmad ibn Abdillah ibn al-Husayn, known as Ibn Kurdi, narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Sa'id al-Maqburi narrated to us, from Ata, freedman of Abu Ahmad, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition of men of number, and examined each man among them in the Qur'an - or he said: From the Qur'an - until he came to a man among the youngest of them in age and said: What do you have, O so-and-so? He said: I have such-and-such and Surah al-Baqarah. He said: You have Surah al-Baqarah? He said: Yes. He said: Go - I think he said: For you are their commander. A man said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, nothing prevented me from learning the Qur'an except fear that I would not uphold it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Recite it and sleep upon it; the likeness of the Qur'an for one who learns it, recites it, and stands by it is like a bag stuffed full whose scent spreads everywhere; and the likeness of one who learns it and sleeps while it is in his belly is like a bag tied shut over musk. We do not know this hadith narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from the hadith of Abu Hurayrah with this chain; and Ata, freedman of Abu Ahmad - we do not know that he narrated from Abu Hurayrah except this hadith, nor that anyone narrated from him except Sa'id al-Maqburi."
"8408","Ata, freedman of Umm Subayyah, from Abu Hurayrah. 8403 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Ata, freedman of Umm Subayyah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Were it not that I would burden my ummah. [The sentence is cut off here in the source row.]"
"8409","Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, from Abu Hurayrah. 8404 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Jabbar, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The womb is a branch stemming from the Most Merciful, saying: O my Lord, I have been wronged; O my Lord, I have been cut off; O my Lord. Its Lord, Blessed and Exalted, answers it, saying: Are you not pleased that I join whoever joins you and cut off whoever cuts you off. We do not know that Muhammad ibn Ka'b narrated as musnad from Abu Hurayrah except this hadith."
"8410","Abu Salih, freedman of Uthman ibn Affan, from Abu Hurayrah. 8405 - Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, from Zuhrah ibn Ma'bad, from Abu Salih, freedman of Uthman ibn Affan, from Uthman and Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever dies guarding the frontier in the path of Allah, the reward of the fasting person's deeds continues for him, his provision continues for him, he is safe from the testers, and Allah raises him on the Day of Resurrection safe from the greatest terror. We do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurayrah except from this angle; we do not know that Abu Salih, freedman of Uthman, narrated from Abu Hurayrah except this hadith; and the name of Abu Salih, freedman of Uthman, is al-Harith."
"8411","Abu Salih, freedman of the Junda'iyyin, from Abu Hurairah. 8406 - Muhammad ibn Humayd wrote to me mentioning that Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to him from Ibn Lahi'ah, from Abu al-Aswad, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Salih who is the freedman of the Junda'iyyin, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prize race except in khuff (camels) or hafir (horses). And we do not know that this Abu Salih narrated with an isnad except this hadith from Abu Hurairah, and none narrated from him except Sulayman ibn Yasar."
"8412","Abu Salih al-Sa'idi, from Abu Hurairah. 8407 - Khalid ibn Yusuf ibn Khalid al-Samti narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us from Hashim ibn Hashim, he said: Abu Salih al-Sa'idi narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Some men will flee to their tribes, while Madinah is better for them if they only knew. By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, no one remains firm in it and endures its hardship and severity except that I will be an intercessor and witness for him on the Day of Resurrection. And no one leaves it out of aversion to it except that Allah will replace in his place one who is better than him. By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, it expels the filth of its people - I think he said - just as the bellows expels the filth of iron. And we do not know that Abu Salih al-Sa'idi narrated with an isnad from Abu Hurairah except this hadith, and none narrated from him except Hashim ibn Hashim, and no name is known for this Abu Salih."
"8413","Ziyad ibn Thuwayb, and it is said Thawb, from Abu Hurairah. 8408 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from Ziyad ibn Thuwayb, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to visit me when I was ill and said: Shall I not perform ruqyah for you with a ruqyah with which Jibril performed ruqyah for me? I said: Yes, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you. So he said: In the name of Allah I perform ruqyah for you, from every disease in you, from the blowers in knots, and from the evil of an envier when he envies."
"8414","Abu Habibah from Abu Hurairah. 8409 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Khalid narrated to us from Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Habibah, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah mentioned a fitnah and brought it near; so we said: O Messenger of Allah, if we reach it, with whom should we be? He said: With the trustworthy one and his companions, Uthman ibn Affan. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Abu Hurairah except Abu Habibah, and Musa ibn Uqbah narrated from Abu Habibah."
"8415","Yahya ibn al-Nadr from Abu Hurairah. 8410 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Aswad narrated to me from Yahya ibn al-Nadr, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever acquires a dog other than for crops or udders (livestock), or a hunting dog, a qirat is deducted from his reward every day."
"8416","Ibrahim ibn Abi Asid from his grandfather, from Abu Hurairah. 8411 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us from Ibrahim ibn Abi Asid, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, you will surely follow the ways of those before you, span by span and cubit by cubit, until if they entered the hole of a lizard you would enter it."
"8417","8412 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us from Ibrahim ibn Abi Asid, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of envy, for it consumes good deeds just as fire consumes firewood."
"8418","Sa'id ibn Sam'an, from Abu Hurairah. 8413 - Abdullah ibn Sa'id Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us from Sa'id ibn Sam'an, from Abu Hurairah who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began the prayer, he spread his fingers in a spreading."
"8419","8414 - And Amr ibn Ali narrated to us - as I think, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Sa'id ibn Sam'an, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to raise his hands extended when he entered the prayer, and he used to remain silent before the recitation asking Allah from His bounty, and he used to say takbir when he lowered and when he raised."
"8420","8415 - And Amr narrated it to us, as I think, from Yahya or from Abu Asim."
"8421","Abu Ghatfan from Abu Hurairah. 8416 - Isma'il ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ya'qub ibn Utbah, from Abu Ghatfan, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever gestures in his prayer with a gesture that is understood from him, let him repeat his prayer, or it has been invalidated - he said: And he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tasbih is for men, and clapping is for women."
"8422","Humayd ibn Malik, from Abu Hurairah. 8417 - Bishr ibn Mu'adh al-Aqadi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ja'far ibn Najih narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Halhalah narrated to us from Wahb ibn Kaysan, from Humayd ibn Malik, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about prayer in sheep pens. He said: Wipe away its nasal discharge and pray in its resting place, for it is among the animals of Paradise. And we do not know that Humayd ibn Malik narrated with an isnad from Abu Hurairah except this hadith."
"8423","What Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi narrated from his father from Abu Hurairah. Ubaydullah from Sa'id from his father. 8418 - Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Habib ibn Yahya al-Raqqi informed us, he said: Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Ubaydullah, meaning Ibn Umar, from Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who are the most noble of people? He said: The most God-fearing of them. They said: It is not about this that we ask you. He said: Then you ask about the mines of the Arabs; the best of them in Jahiliyyah are the best of them in Islam when they attain understanding."
"8424","8419 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id narrated to us from his father, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque, then a man entered and prayed, then he came and greeted the Messenger of Allah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned the greeting and said: Go back and pray, for you have not prayed. So he went back and prayed as he had prayed, then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and greeted him; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go back and pray, for you have not prayed. He did that three times, then he said: By the One Who sent you with the truth, I cannot do better than this, so teach me. He said: When you stand for prayer, say takbir, then recite what is easy for you of the Qur'an, then bow until you are tranquil while bowing, then rise until you stand upright, then prostrate until you are tranquil while prostrating, then rise until you are tranquil while sitting, then do that in all of your prayer."
"8425","8420 - And Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah, he said: Sa'id narrated to me from his father, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Women are married for four: for her wealth, for her lineage, and for her religion, so hold to the one with religion, may your hands be covered in dust. And these hadiths which Yahya narrated from Ubaydullah, from Sa'id, from his father, others narrate them from Ubaydullah, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah."
"8426","8421 - Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Abu Damrah Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah narrated to us from Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When one of you comes to his bed, let him take the inner part of his lower garment and shake his bed with it, then say: In Your name I lay my side and by You I raise it; if You withhold it (my soul) then have mercy on it, and if You release it then guard it with what You guard Your righteous servants. And this hadith was narrated by more than one from Ubaydullah, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah, while Abu Damrah said from Sa'id, from his father."
"8427","Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Sa'id, from his father. 8422 - al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that I would impose hardship on my ummah, I would have made the siwak obligatory at every prayer. And this hadith was narrated by Abu Ubaydullah from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah."
"8428","8423 - al-Hasan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, exalted is His praise, will surely send down Isa ibn Maryam as a just judge and an equitable imam, and he will surely travel the Rawha' as a pilgrim."
"8429","8424 - And al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id narrated to us from his father, from Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer, and there was a man in the last rows, or he was in the last rows, and he said: O so-and-so, do you not fear Allah? Do you not consider how you pray? When one of you stands to pray, he stands conversing privately with his Lord, so let him consider how he prays. You think that I do not see you; by Allah, I see you from behind my back just as I see from in front of me. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah except Muhammad ibn Ishaq."
"8430","8425 - al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah who said: A Bedouin gave a she-camel as a gift to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) compensated him for it, yet he remained displeased. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and said: Some people give gifts to me, and a man gave me a she-camel from camels I recognize as I recognize some of my family - then he mentioned a phrase as if informing about his rewarding him - yet he remained displeased. By Allah, I will not accept from anyone of the Arabs after this standing of mine except from a Qurashi, or an Ansari, or a Thaqafi, or a Dawsi."
"8431","Ibn Abi Dhi'b from Sa'id al-Maqburi. 8426 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us from Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: O believing women, let none of you belittle anything for her neighbor, even a sheep's trotter, and a woman must not travel except with a mahram."
"8432","8427 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us from Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A woman must not travel a journey of three days except with a mahram."
"8433","8428 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us from Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not abandon false speech and acting upon it, Allah has no need for his abandoning his food and drink."
"8434","8429 - And Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Qutaybah narrated to us from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like of it."
"8435","8430 - And Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us from Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever follows a funeral from its family until he prays over it, he has a qirat, and whoever waits for its burial, he has two qirats."
"8436","8431 - And Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us from Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sneezing is from Allah, and yawning is from Satan, and it is a duty upon whoever hears him (the sneezer) to say: May Allah have mercy on you."
"8437","8432 - al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Shababab ibn Sawwar narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us from Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prays, let him place his sandals between his feet."
"8438","8433 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us from Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sun has neither risen nor set upon a day better than Friday. Allah guided us to it and people strayed from it, so people follow us in it; it is ours, and for the Jews Saturday, and for the Christians Sunday. And in it there is an hour which no believer meets asking Allah for something except that He gives it to him."
"8439","Ibn Ajlan from Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah. 8434 - al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Aruzzi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan, from Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman must not travel three (days) except with a mahram. And the hadith of Ibn Ajlan from Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah is mudtarib (disturbed), because it became confused for him: what he narrated from Sa'id from Abu Hurairah, and what he narrated from Sa'id from his father. So Ibn Ajlan narrated from Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah three disturbed hadiths, this is one of them, and among them:"
"8440","8435 - What al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah ibn al-Bazzar al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan, from Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When one of you steps with his khuffs or sandals upon something, their purification is the dust. And this hadith was narrated by others than al-Awza'i from Ibn Ajlan from al-Maqburi from a man, and the hadith is not established."
"8441","8436 - And I found in my book from Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar, he said: Abu Hisham narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: O Muslim women, let no neighbor belittle (a gift) to her neighbor, even a sheep's trotter. And this hadith is only preserved from the hadith of Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah; as for Ibn Ajlan, it is not preserved from him from Sa'id from his father."
"8442","8437 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Kathir narrated to us from Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar, from al-Maqburi, from his father, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the worst forms of riba is a man's extending (his tongue) against the honor of his brother. And I think this hadith is a mistake, because Salih only narrated it in my view from Abdullah ibn Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, since Salih did not hear from Sa'id al-Maqburi; but thus Yahya ibn Kathir narrated it from Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar from al-Maqburi."
"8443","al-Layth ibn Sa'd from Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah. 8438 - Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us, he said: Shababah ibn Sawwar narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: There is no god but Allah alone; He aided His servant and overcame the confederates alone, so there is nothing after Him. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurairah except from this channel."
"8444","8439 - And Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us, he said: Shababah ibn Sawwar informed us from al-Layth ibn Sa'd, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no prophet among the prophets except that he was given of the signs the like of which - I think he said - belief is affirmed upon; and what I was given was revelation which Allah revealed to me, so I hope to be the one with the most followers on the Day of Resurrection."
"8445","8440 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, he said: al-Maqburi narrated to us from Layth, meaning Ibn Sa'd, from Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"8446","8441 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us from Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: In Paradise there is a tree under whose shade a rider travels for a hundred years."
"8447","8442 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: al-Maqburi narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us from Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a Muslim woman to travel three (days) except with a mahram."
"8448","8443 - al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Ilyas narrated to us from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not tire until you tire, and the most beloved deeds to Allah are the most constant even if few. Adhere to of the matter what you can bear."
"8449","8444 - al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muqatil al-Qushayri narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Qudamah al-Jumahi narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Bakr narrated to us from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from his father, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The hypocrites have signs by which they are known: their greeting is curse, their food is plunder, their spoils are ghulul (misappropriation). They do not come to the mosques except in aversion, and they do not come to prayer except at the end. Logs by night, noisy by day. And we do not know this hadith narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this channel with this isnad, and we do not know anyone who narrated from Ishaq ibn Bakr except Abd al-Malik ibn Qudamah."
"8450","8445 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us from his grandfather, from Abu Hurairah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting six days of the year: the day of Adha, the day of Fitr, the days of Tashriq, and the day of doubt concerning Ramadan."
"8451","8446 - Muhammad ibn al-Layth narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Nahshali narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Sa'id, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted, has creatures He spreads through the night, so cover your vessels, tie your waterskins, and close your doors, for no cover is uncovered and no door opened."
"8452","8447 - And with his isnad: A man may speak a word to make people laugh with it, and he falls with it farther than al-Thurayya (the Pleiades)."
"8453","And of what Sa'id al-Maqburi narrated from Abu Hurairah: what Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah. 8448 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah, meaning Ibn Umar, narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to me from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the most noble of people? He said: The most God-fearing of them toward Allah. They said: It is not about this that we ask you. He said: Then you ask about the mines of the Arabs? They said: Yes. He said: The best of you in Jahiliyyah are the best of you in Islam when they attain understanding."
"8454","8449 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us from Ubaydullah, meaning Ibn Umar, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade a town-dweller selling for a Bedouin."
"8455","8450 - Ubayd ibn Isma'il al-Habbari narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us from Ubaydullah, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that I would impose hardship on my ummah, I would have commanded them with the siwak at every prayer, and I would have delayed the Isha prayer to the first third of the night - or to the half, the doubt is from Ubaydullah - for Allah, blessed and exalted, when the first third of the night - or its half - has passed, descends to the lowest heaven and calls out: Is there any supplicant so I may answer? Is there any seeker of forgiveness so I may forgive him? Or any asker so I may give him? Until dawn rises."
"8456","8451 - And Hudbah narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Ubaydullah, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"8457","8452 - And Ubayd ibn Isma'il al-Habbari narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us from Ubaydullah, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah has made sacred what is between the two lava tracts of Madinah - I think he said - upon my tongue. Then he came - I think he said - to Banu Harithah and said: I see you as having left it. Then he looked and said: Rather, you are within it."
"8458","8453 - And Bishr ibn Adam and al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated to us, they said: al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four Allah hates: the swearing seller, the arrogant poor man, the fornicating old man, and the treacherous imam (ruler). And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"8459","8454 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la informed us, he said: Ubaydullah narrated to us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah, and from Nafi' from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A woman entered the Fire concerning a cat she tied up; she neither fed it nor let it eat from the vermin of the earth."
"8460","8455 - Ubayd ibn Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us from Ubaydullah, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When the slave-girl of one of you commits zina, let him flog her; then if she commits zina, let him flog her; then if she commits zina, let him sell her even for a rope of palm fiber."
"8461","8456 - Ubayd ibn Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us from Ubaydullah, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat - I think he said - and whoever waits for it until it is buried has two qirats."
"8462","8457 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Raja' al-Makki, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever performs ghusl on Friday, wears his best clothes, comes early, does not separate between two, prays what was written for him, and when the imam comes out listens and is silent, he will have (forgiveness) between it and the next Friday."
"8463","8458 - Yahya ibn Yazid al-Ahwazi wrote to me mentioning that Abu Hammam narrated to him, he said: Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One of the prophets undertook a military expedition after Asr. He said: No man who built a building and has not finished it shall follow me, or undertake expedition with me, nor a man who married a woman and has not consummated with her. He said: And there remained of the sun only a little. He said: O Allah, the sun is commanded and I am commanded; O Allah, withhold it. So Allah withheld it for an hour until Allah granted him victory. Then he ordered the spoils and they were gathered, and fire came but did not consume them. So he said: There is ghulul among you; let a man from every tribe come to me and pledge to me. So his hand stuck to the hand of a man or two men. So he said: The ghulul is among you, so bring it out. So they brought out a cow's head of gold and cast it into the spoils - then it consumed it, I think he said: the fire - So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Spoils were not lawful for anyone before us, and that is because Allah saw our weakness and made them wholesome for us. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah except Mubarak ibn Fadalah. And it was narrated from Sa'id from Ajlan, and Ma'mar narrated it from Hammam, from Abu Hurairah, and Qatadah narrated it from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurairah."
"8464","8459 - Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Hubayb, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurairah, and from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah, one of them raising it (to the Prophet): Allah, blessed and exalted, accepts charity, and He accepts of it only the wholesome, and He nurtures it just as one of you raises his young camel or foal."
"8465","8460 - Salamah ibn Shabib and Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, and the wording is Zuhayr's - he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar informed us from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah: that Thumamah ibn Uthal embraced Islam, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to perform ghusl with water and sidr (lote). And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah except Abd al-Razzaq."
"8466","8461 - And Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah narrated to us from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will fight a people whose faces are as if hammered shields."
"8467","What Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah. 8462 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi al-Shawarib al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the deceased - or one of you - is taken in death, two angels, black and blue-eyed, come to him, one called al-Munkar and the other al-Nakir, and they say: What did you used to say about this man? So he says: The servant of Allah and His Messenger; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. So they say: We knew that you used to say this. Then his grave is expanded for him seventy cubits by seventy cubits, then it is illuminated for him in it, then it is said to him: Sleep until you return to your family. He said: So he sleeps like the sleep of one whom none awakens except the dearest of his family to him, until Allah resurrects him from that resting place. He said: Then the disbeliever is brought and it is said: What did you used to say about this man? He says: I saw people saying something so I said it. So they say: We knew that you would say that. Then it is said to the earth: Close upon him. So it closes upon him, and his ribs differ within it, and he remains in it tormented until Allah resurrects him from that resting place. And we do not know this hadith narrated with this wording from Abu Hurairah except from this channel."
"8468","8463 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not love waste of wealth, excessive asking, nor qila (it was said) nor qala (he said)."
"8469","8464 - And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Bishr narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the slave-girl of one of you commits zina, let him flog her, and when she commits zina, let him flog her - three times - then sell her even for a rope."
"8470","8465 - And Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Bishr narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May the nose of a man be rubbed in dust before whom I am mentioned and he does not invoke blessings upon me; may the nose of a man be rubbed in dust who reaches his parents in old age and they do not admit him into Paradise; and may the nose of a man be rubbed in dust upon whom Ramadan enters then passes from him without his being forgiven."
"8471","8466 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three Allah will not look at on the Day of Resurrection: the fornicating old man, the lying imam (ruler), and the arrogant destitute. Yazid said: The arrogant destitute is the boastful poor man."
"8472","8467 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Five are of the fitrah: circumcision, shaving the pubic hair, plucking the armpit, clipping the nails, and trimming the mustache."
"8473","8468 - Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Rawwas narrated to us, he said: Hatim ibn Wardan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Wealth is not from abundance of goods, but wealth is wealth of the soul."
"8474","Amr ibn Abi Amr, freedman of al-Muttalib, from Abu Hurairah. 8469 - Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, who are the happiest of people with your intercession on the Day of Resurrection? He said: I thought no one would ask me about this hadith other than you, because of what I saw of your eagerness for knowledge - as I think - The happiest of people with my intercession on the Day of Resurrection is whoever says: There is no god but Allah, sincerely from before himself."
"8475","8470 - Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Many a standing one whose share of his standing is wakefulness, and many a fasting one whose share of his fasting is hunger and thirst."
"8476","8471 - Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, raising it (to the Prophet): The believer is with Me in the station of all good; he praises Me while I take his soul from between his sides."
"8477","8472 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Sulayman al-Numayri informed us from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever undertakes judgeship, or is made a judge - has been slaughtered without a knife."
"8478","Zayd ibn Aslam from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah. 8473 - Muhammad ibn Sufyan ibn Abi al-Zarad al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us from Zayd ibn Aslam, from al-Maqburi - he once said from Ibn al-Maqburi, and the correct is from al-Maqburi - from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is made a judge has been slaughtered without a knife. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Zayd except al-Thawri, nor from al-Thawri except Bakr ibn Bakkar."
"8479","8474 - Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah who said: I came to al-Tur (Sinai) and Humayl ibn Basrah met me and said to me: From where have you come? I said: From al-Tur. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere; so had you prayed in this mosque it would have been better for you, and had I met you before you went I would not have let you go to it."
"8480","Malik ibn Anas from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah. 8475 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A time will surely come upon people when a man will not care - I think he said - with what he takes wealth, whether lawful or unlawful."
"8481","8476 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has an injustice against his brother with him, let him come to him and seek his absolution before it is taken while he has neither dinar nor dirham; if he has good deeds, they will be taken from his good deeds, otherwise they will be taken from the evil deeds of this one and placed upon his evil deeds."
"8482","8477 - And Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to travel a day except with a mahram from her family."
"8483","Ibn Abi Dhubab from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah. 8478 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, they said: Safwan narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhubab narrated to us from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah, blessed and exalted, created Adam and breathed the spirit into him, he sneezed and said: Praise be to Allah, by Allah's permission. So his Lord said to him: May your Lord have mercy on you, O Adam. Then He said: Go to those group of angels sitting and say: Peace be upon you. So they said: And upon you peace and the mercy of Allah. Then he returned to his Lord, blessed and exalted, and He said: This is your greeting and the greeting of your offspring among them. Then He said to him, while His two hands were closed: Choose whichever of them you wish. So he said: I choose the right hand of my Lord, and both hands of my Lord are right and blessed. Then He extended it, and in it were Adam and his offspring, and the lifespan of every human among them was written with Him, and Adam had a thousand years, and among them were men upon whom was light, and among them a man the most radiant of them, or among the most radiant of them, for whom only forty years were written. He said: My Lord, who is this? He said: This is your son Dawud. He said: My Lord, increase his lifespan. He said: That is what I wrote for him. So he said: I deduct for him sixty years from my lifespan. He said: You and that. Then Adam was settled in Paradise as long as Allah willed, then he was sent down from it, and he used to count for himself. Then the Angel of Death came to him and he said: You hastened; did Allah not write a thousand years for me? He said: Yes, but you gave sixty years of it to your son Dawud. He said: I did not do it. He said: So he denied, and his offspring denied; and he forgot, and his offspring forgot. So on that day writing and witnesses were commanded. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah, except al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman."
"8484","Uthman ibn Muhammad al-Akhnasi from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah. 8479 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us, he said: Mu'alla ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ja'far, meaning al-Mukharrimi, narrated to us from Uthman ibn Muhammad, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It will surely quiver with you like the quivering of a young camel - meaning: the earth. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurairah except from this channel with this isnad."
"8485","8480 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Mu'alla ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us from Uthman ibn Muhammad, from al-Maqburi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he cursed the muhill (one who marries to make lawful) and the one for whom it is made lawful. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurairah except from this channel with this isnad."
"8486","8481 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Mu'alla ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us from Uthman ibn Muhammad, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Beware of injustice, for injustice is darknesses on the Day of Resurrection."
"8487","8482 - Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Mu'alla ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us from Uthman ibn Muhammad, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Beware of evil discord between people, for it is the shaver."
"8488","8483 - And Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Mu'alla ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us from Uthman ibn Muhammad, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I enjoin the rights of the two weak ones: the woman and the orphan."
"8489","8484 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us: Bishr ibn Umar informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us from Uthman ibn Muhammad, from al-Maqburi and Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whoever is made a judge has been slaughtered without a knife."
"8490","8485 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from his father Muhammad ibn Mu'awiyah, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, from Uthman ibn Muhammad, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah, raising it (to the Prophet): What is between the east and the west is qiblah. And we do not know anyone who raised it except Muhammad ibn Mu'awiyah, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, from Uthman."
"8491","What Ibn Ajlan narrated from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah. 8486 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Beware of obscenity, for Allah does not love obscenity nor being obscene; and beware of injustice, for injustice is darknesses on the Day of Resurrection; and beware of miserliness, for it destroyed those before you: it commanded them to shed their blood and they shed their blood, and commanded them to sever their kinship and they severed, and commanded them and they deemed their sacred things lawful."
"8492","8487 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not the Bedouins overcome you over the name of your prayer, meaning the Isha prayer."
"8493","8488 - And Amr narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I enjoin the rights of the two weak ones: the woman and the orphan."
"8494","8489 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two branches of the affair of Jahiliyyah people will not abandon: wailing, and defamation of lineages."
"8495","8490 - And Amr narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give charity. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a dinar. He said: Give it in charity upon yourself. He said: I have another. He said: Give it in charity upon your wife. He said: I have another. He said: Give it in charity upon your child. He said: I have another. He said: Give it in charity upon your servant. He said: I have another. He said: You know best. And we do not know this hadith narrated except from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this isnad. And al-Thawri narrated it from Ibn Ajlan."
"8496","8491 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us: A man asked Abu Hurairah: How much suffices of ghusl from janabah? He said: Pour upon your head three times. He said: My hair is thick. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had more hair than you and better."
"8497","8492 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us from Abu Hurairah, and from his father from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no commander of ten except that he will be brought bound on the Day of Resurrection until justice frees him or tyranny destroys him. And we do not know anyone who combined Ibn Ajlan from Sa'id and Ibn Ajlan from his father from Abu Hurairah except Yahya ibn Sa'id."
"8498","8493 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Qays al-Madani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah, and from Ibn Ajlan, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever wrongfully takes a span of land will be collared with it on the Day of Resurrection from seven earths. And we do not know anyone who combined Ibn Ajlan and his father from Sa'id from Abu Hurairah except Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Qays."
"8499","8494 - And Amr narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to travel a journey - I do not know how much he said its distance - except with a mahram."
"8500","8495 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting with Abu Bakr with him, when a man began insulting Abu Bakr while the Messenger of Allah smiled. When he did so excessively, Abu Bakr returned some of his words upon him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up angry. Abu Bakr caught up with him and said: O Messenger of Allah, he insulted me while you listened, then when I responded you stood and left me! He said: An angel was responding to him, but when you responded, Satan came, and I would not sit with Satan."
"8501","8496 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from an evil neighbor in the abode of residence, for the neighbor of the desert moves on."
"8502","8497 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat, and whoever follows it until its matter is concluded has two qirats."
"8503","8498 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Bakka'i narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: Muhammad al-Ansari narrated to us from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Return the invocation for the sneezer three times; if he exceeds, then it is a cold."
"8504","8499 - Bishr ibn Mu'adh al-Aqadi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ja'far ibn Najih narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When you see the flatterers, throw dust in their faces. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurairah except from this channel with this isnad."
"8505","8500 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three Allah is bound to aid: the mujahid in the path of Allah, the one who marries to remain chaste, and the mukatab (contracted slave) who seeks payment."
"8506","8501 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you reaches a gathering, let him give salam; and when he wishes to stand, let him give salam; the first is not more deserving than the last."
"8507","8502 - And Sa'id ibn Bahr al-Qaratisiyy narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us from Ibn Uyaynah, from Ibn Ajlan, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah, raising it (to the Prophet). He said: May Allah have mercy on a man who stands at night and wakes his wife; if she refuses, he sprinkles water on her face. May Allah have mercy on a woman who stands at night, prays, and wakes her husband; if he refuses, she sprinkles water on his face. And the companions of Ibn Ajlan only narrate this hadith from al-Qa'qa', from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah; while Husayn said from Ibn Uyaynah, from Ibn Ajlan, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah."
"8508","8503 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he intended travel said: O Allah, You are the Companion in travel and the Successor over the family. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the hardship of travel, the gloom of return, and the evil sight in family and wealth. O Allah, fold the earth for us and ease travel for us."
"8509","8504 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you strikes, let him avoid the face; let him not say: May Allah disgrace your face and the face of whoever resembles your face, for Allah, blessed and exalted, created Adam upon his image."
"8510","8505 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to me from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever attends a funeral among its family and prays over it has a qirat, and whoever follows it until its matter is concluded has two qirats."
"8511","8506 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When one of you rises at night from his bed then returns to it, he does not know what was left in it after him, so let him shake it with his lower garment or part of his lower garment. Then when he lies down, let him say: In Your name I lay my side and by You I raise it; if You withhold my soul, forgive it, and if You release it, guard it with what You guard Your righteous servants."
"8512","8507 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah, who said: A man gave a milch camel as a gift to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he rewarded him for it with six young camels, yet he remained displeased. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So-and-so gave me a milch camel and I rewarded him for it with six young camels, yet he remained displeased - or discontented - By Allah, I intended not to accept a gift from an Arab man unless he be Qurashi, or Ansari, or Dawsi, or Thaqafi."
"8513","8508 - And Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted, loves sneezing and hates yawning; when one of you yawns, that is only Satan laughing from his belly."
"8514","8509 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: None endures its hardship (Madinah's) except that I will be an intercessor or witness for him."
"8515","8510 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Yahya ibn Zabban narrated to us, he said: Hibban ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: You shall surely command the good and forbid the evil, or Allah will surely empower your wicked over you, then your best will supplicate and will not be answered. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurairah except from this channel."
"8516","8511 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah created Adam, his length sixty cubits."
"8517","Ibn Abi Dhi'b from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah. 8512 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave salam in two rak'ahs. So they said: O Messenger of Allah, did you forget or was the prayer shortened? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I did not forget and the prayer was not shortened. They said: O Messenger of Allah, you forgot. So he bowed two other rak'ahs and prostrated two prostrations."
"8518","8513 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah he does not believe, by Allah he does not believe: a neighbor whose neighbor is not safe from his evils. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what are his evils? He said: His evil."
"8519","8514 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The seven oft-repeated are the Opening of the Book (al-Fatihah)."
"8520","8515 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah he does not believe - three times - whoever whose neighbor is not safe from his evils. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what are his evils? He said: His evil."
"8521","8516 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah who said: By Allah, I am the most knowledgeable of you of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head from bowing he said: O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise; and he used to say takbir when he rose, when he lowered, and when he raised."
"8522","8517 - Muhammad ibn Juwan ibn Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Buhlul ibn Muwarriq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah, who said: I memorized from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - I think he said - two pouches; as for one of them, I spread it among people, and as for the other, had I spread it my throat would be cut."
"8523","8518 - Muhammad ibn Juwan narrated to us, he said: Buhlul narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until - I think he said - this ummah takes the ways of those before it, span by span and cubit by cubit. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As Persia and Rome did."
"8524","8519 - Salamah ibn Shabib and Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not know whether the hudud (prescribed punishments) are expiations or not?! And I do not know whether Tubba' was accursed or not?! And I do not know whether Uzayr was a prophet or not! And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ibn Abi Dhi'b except Ma'mar."
"8525","Suhayl ibn Abi Salih from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah. 8520 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, he said: Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to us from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah who said: A woman must not travel a barid (postal distance) except with a mahram. Bishr said: I think he raised it (to the Prophet). And we do not know that Suhayl narrated with an isnad from al-Maqburi except this hadith."
"8526","Abu Hazim from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah. 8521 - Hisham ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us from his father, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The age in which Allah excuses the son of Adam is sixty years - meaning: Did We not give you life long enough for whoever would remember to remember therein."
"8527","Muhammad ibn Amr from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah. 8522 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One of you gives a date in charity when it is from wholesome (earnings), and Allah accepts only the wholesome, so He nurtures it just as one of you raises his foal until it returns in his hand like a mountain. And we do not know that Muhammad ibn Amr narrated with an isnad from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah, except this hadith."
"8528","al-Dahhak ibn Uthman al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah. 8523 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: al-Maqburi narrated to us from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you enters the mosque, let him send salam upon the Prophet and say: O Allah, open for me the doors of Your mercy; and when he leaves, let him send salam and say: O Allah, protect me from evil."
"8529","8524 - Ahmad ibn al-Faraj al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, he said: al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to us from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah who said: Safwan ibn al-Mu'attal asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Are there among the hours of night and day an hour in which prayer is disliked? He said: Yes; when you pray Fajr, leave prayer until the sun rises, for it rises between the two horns of Satan. Then pray, the prayer accepted, until the sun stands over your head like a spear. When it is over your head like a spear, leave prayer, for that is the hour in which Hell is stoked and its doors opened, until the sun declines from your right eyebrow. When it declines or passes its zenith, prayer is attended and accepted until you pray Asr, then leave prayer until the sun sets."
"8530","Uthman ibn Murrah from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah. 8525 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Murrah narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id narrated to us from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you cleans with stones (istinjar), let him make it odd. And we do not know that Uthman ibn Murrah narrated with an isnad from al-Maqburi except this hadith."
"8531","Hisham ibn Sa'd from al-Maqburi. 8526 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Sa'd al-Rahhal narrated to us from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted, has removed from you the pride of Jahiliyyah and boasting of fathers. People are the children of Adam, and Adam is from dust. Men shall surely abandon their boasting of peoples who are but coal from the coal of Hell, or they shall be more insignificant to Allah than the dung beetles that push filth with their noses. And this hadith was disputed over from Hisham ibn Sa'd in it; al-Mu'afa ibn Imran narrated it from Hisham ibn Sa'd, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from his father, from Abu Hurairah and others, and others followed him upon it with this isnad, while more than one narrated it from Hisham ibn Sa'd, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah."
"8532","Ayyub ibn Musa, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah. 8527 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, he said: Hisham, meaning Ibn Hassan, narrated to us from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When the slave-girl of one of you commits zina, let him flog her; then if she commits zina, let him flog her; then if she commits zina, let him flog her; then if she commits zina, let him sell her even for a braid of hair. And we do not know that Ayyub ibn Musa narrated with an isnad from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah, except this hadith and another hadith disputed in it."
"8533","Usamah ibn Zayd, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah. 8528 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, he said: Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intending travel and said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me. He said: I advise you with fear of Allah and takbir upon every elevation. When he turned away - or he said departed - he said: O Allah, fold the earth for him and ease travel for him."
"8534","8529 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, he said: Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When the slave-girl of one of you commits zina, let him flog her; then if she commits zina, let him sell her even for a braid."
"8535","Abd al-Rahman ibn Wardan, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah. 8530 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Wardan narrated to us from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Isa ibn Maryam will descend as a just judge and equitable imam to break the cross, kill the pig, and the qiblah will become one."
"8536","Abu Ma'shar, from al-Maqburi. 8531 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Jabir ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On the Day of Resurrection a man will be called by his most abundant deed; if prayer was best, he will be called by it, and if his fasting was best, he will be called by it, and if jihad was best, he will be called by it. Then he comes to a gate of Paradise called al-Rayyan from which the fasting ones are called. Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said: O Messenger of Allah, is there anyone called by two deeds? He said: Yes, you."
"8537","8532 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Jabir ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us from Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what is isbagh (thoroughness)? So he remained silent until prayer time came, then he called for water and poured upon his hand, then washed his face and hands three times, wiped his head, washed his feet three times, and sprinkled beneath his garment, then said: Such is the thoroughness of wudu."
"8538","8533 - And Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Jabir ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I shall surely know one of you reclining when a hadith comes to him from me while he reclines on his couch, saying: Recite upon me a Qur'an; whatever of good comes to you that I said, and if I did not say it then I say it; and whatever of evil comes to you, for I do not speak evil. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurairah except with this isnad."
"8539","8534 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Jabir ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from deafness and dumbness, and I seek refuge in You from sin and debt, and I seek refuge in You from distress - meaning: drowning - and I seek refuge in You from old age, and I seek refuge in You from hunger, for it is an evil bedfellow, and I seek refuge in You from treachery, for it is an evil inner lining. And we do not know this hadith narrated with this completeness from Abu Hurairah except from this channel with this isnad."
"8540","8535 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Jabir ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: You shall surely take (the ways) as the nations before you took - or a phrase like it - cubit by cubit, span by span, and fathom by fathom, until if one of those entered the hole of a lizard you would enter it, or you would enter them."
"8541","8536 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Jabir ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah who said: A crescent then a crescent would pass over the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) without a fire being kindled in any of his houses for bread or cooking. He said: With what did they live, O Abu Hurairah? He said: With the two black ones: dates and water; and he had neighbors from the Ansar, may Allah reward them with good, who had milch animals and would send to them some milk."
"8542","8537 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us from Sa'id, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of women is a woman who, when you look at her, pleases you; when you command her, obeys you; and when you are absent from her, guards you in herself and your wealth. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurairah except from this channel with this isnad."
"8543","Abdullah ibn Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah. 8538 - al-Harith ibn al-Khadir al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Sa'd ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi narrated to us from his brother Abdullah ibn Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Riba is seventy sins, the lightest of them - or the lightest of it - like one who falls upon his mother; and the worst of riba is the honor of the Muslim."
"8544","8539 - And al-Harith ibn al-Khadir narrated to us, he said: Sa'd ibn Sa'id narrated to us from his brother, from his father, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no share in Islam for one who has no prayer, and no prayer for one who has no wudu."
"8545","8540 - al-Harith ibn al-Khadir narrated to us, he said: Sa'd ibn Sa'id narrated to us from his brother Abdullah ibn Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the right of the child upon the parent is that he give him a good name and good upbringing."
"8546","8541 - al-Harith ibn al-Khadir narrated to us, he said: Sa'd ibn Sa'id narrated to us from his brother Abdullah ibn Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not know whether the hudud are expiation for their people or not? And I do not know whether Uzayr was a prophet or not? And I do not know whether Tubba' is accursed or not?"
"8547","8542 - al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us from his brother, from his father, from Abu Hurairah - I think he raised it (to the Prophet) - he said: When you are reminded of Allah, then desist."
"8548","8543 - al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Sa'd narrated to us from his brother, from his father, from Abu Hurairah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes to the mosque, let him send salam upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and say: O Allah, open for me the doors of Your mercy; and when he leaves, let him send salam upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and say: O Allah, protect me from Satan."
"8549","8544 - al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Malik al-Muzani narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Sa'id al-Maqburi, from his father, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will never encompass people with your wealth, but what encompasses them from you is cheerfulness of face and good character."
"8550","8545 - And Bishr ibn Mu'adh al-Aqadi narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us from his father, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Your oath is upon what your companion believes you in."
"8551","8546 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us from his father, from Abu Hurairah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) employed al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami over Bahrain and had Abu Hurairah follow him, so he stipulated upon him that he be a mu'adhdhin and not precede him with Amin. And these hadiths which Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated, we do not know anyone who followed him in his narration from al-Maqburi, nor are they preserved from Abu Hurairah from other than this channel except two hadiths of them which we mentioned, so we repeated them from Abdullah ibn Sa'id from his father due to the rarity of their outlet."
"8552","al-Layth from Sa'id. 8547 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih Abu Salih narrated to us: al-Layth informed us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Recite the two radiant ones; recite Surat al-Baqarah and Al Imran, for they will come on the Day of Resurrection as if two clouds, or two shades and flocks of birds in ranks. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah, except al-Layth."
"8553","8548 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abu Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - no one would take his hand and pull his hand from his hand until the man was the one who released it; and his knees - or his knee - were not seen protruding beyond the knee of his sitting companion; and no one shook hands with him except that he faced him with his face, then did not turn it from him until he finished his speech."
"8554","8549 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Sinan narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Sulayman narrated to me from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he recited this verse: On that Day it will relate its news, for your Lord inspired it. He said: Do you know what its news is?! Its news is that it testifies against every servant, male and female, for what he did upon its back; it says: He did such and such on such and such day. So these are its news."
"8555","8550 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi al-Wazir Abu al-Mutarrif narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa al-Mu'allim narrated to us from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Excellent is the suhur of the believer: dates. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurairah except from this channel, and Muhammad ibn Musa is a well-known man from the people of Madinah."
"8556","8551 - Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whatever is above the ankles - or below the ankles of the izar - I think he said - is in the Fire, or a wording like it. And we do not know of Shu'bah narrating a musnad report from al-Maqburi except this hadith."
"8557","8552 - Sa'id ibn Bahr al-Qaratisisi narrated to us, he said: Ma'n ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you touches his private part with his hand with no covering or barrier between them, let him perform ablution. And we do not know this hadith reported from Abu Hurairah with this wording except through this route, and Yazid ibn Abd al-Malik is lenient in hadith."
"8558","8553 - And Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abd (al-Malik) narrated to us, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Say 'La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah' often, for it is a treasure from the treasures of Paradise."
"8559","8554 - Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever bathes on Friday, wears the best of his clothes, applies perfume if he has any, goes early and arrives at the beginning, does not separate two people, prays whatever Allah has decreed for him until the imam comes out, then listens and remains silent until the imam finishes, he is forgiven what is between the two Fridays."
"8560","8555 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah: that a bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), halted his mount at the door of the mosque, came until he stood before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: Which of you is the son of Abd al-Muttalib? They said: This fair-skinned one reclining on his arm. He said: O Muhammad, I am going to question you and press you hard in questioning. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ask. He said: I ask you by the Lord of those before you and the Lord of those after you, did Allah send you? He said: O Allah, yes."
"8561","What Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi narrated from Abu Salamah. 8556 - Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ayyub al-Raqqi informed us, he said: Ahmad ibn Umar al-Bazzar narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Abi Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Harrani narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a funeral, and said: O Allah, forgive our living and our dead, our males and our females, our young and our old, our present and our absent. O Allah, whoever of us You keep alive, keep him alive upon faith, and whoever of us You cause to die, cause him to die upon Islam. And we do not know anyone who narrated this from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim except Muhammad ibn Ishaq. And Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated it from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah."
"8562","8557 - al-Hasan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man may utter a word of Allah's wrath, seeing no harm in it, to make his companions laugh, and he falls because of it into Hell for seventy autumns. And we do not know anyone who narrates it from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, except Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, nor from Muhammad except Muhammad ibn Ishaq."
"8563","8558 - And al-Hasan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah - I think he raised it - he said: The Dajjal will descend upon Khuz and Kirman with eighty thousand whose sandals are of hair and whose garments are tayalisah, their faces like hammered shields. And we do not know this hadith reported with this wording except from the hadith of Ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah."
"8564","8559 - And Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Awn narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not tell you of the best of you? They said: Yes. He said: The best of you are the longest-lived among you and the best of you in character. And we do not know this hadith reported from Abu Hurairah with a better chain than this chain with this wording."
"8565","8560 - Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qutai narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prays over a funeral, let him be sincere in supplication for it. And we do not know this hadith reported except from Abu Hurairah, from the hadith of Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, except that Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated it from his father, from Ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib."
"8566","8561 - One of our companions narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever spends a pair in the path of Allah, two dinars or two camels, the keepers of Paradise call him to Paradise: Come. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, that is the one who has no loss upon him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I hope you are among them, O Abu Bakr."
"8567","8562 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Juwayriyah narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, he said: Abu Hurairah narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever spends a pair of his wealth in the path of Allah, the keepers of Paradise call him at every gate of Paradise: Come, approach. Abu Bakr said: That is the one who has no loss upon him - then he mentioned something similar."
"8568","8563 - Ubaydullah ibn Sa'd ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: My uncle Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to me, he said: My father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The acts of cleanliness are four: trimming the mustache, shaving the pubic hair, plucking the armpit, and clipping the nails."
"8569","8564 - Muhammad ibn Umar al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Abu Damrah Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn al-Had narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah: that a drunkard was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Beat him. They beat him, some striking with the hand, with the garment, and with the sandal. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his companions: Reproach him. They turned to the man saying: Did you not fear Allah? Did you not dread Allah? Were you not ashamed before Allah? Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave him. And we do not know this hadith reported with this wording except from Abu Hurairah with this chain."
"8570","8565 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has never permitted anything as He has permitted a prophet with a beautiful voice chanting the Quran."
"8571","8566 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah: that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: What do you think, if there were a river at the door of one of you in which he bathes five times every day, would any of his dirt remain? They said: None of his dirt would remain. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then the example of the five prayers is like that; they wipe away sins."
"8572","Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Abu Salamah. 8567 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Fadalah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to me, from Bakr ibn Amr, from Safwan ibn Sulaym - Bakr said: I think - from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When you leave your home, pray two rak'ahs that protect you from an evil exit, and when you enter your home, pray two rak'ahs that protect you from an evil entrance. And we do not know this hadith reported from Abu Hurairah except through this route."
"8573","8568 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Abi Hakim, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever washes a dead person, let him bathe."
"8574","8569 - Muhammad ibn Hashim Abu Sahl narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sinan narrated to us, he said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym - he said: I think - from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When women ask your permission to go to the mosques, do not prevent them - I think he said - and let them go out unattractive."
"8575","8570 - And Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Suhban narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Three eyes will not enter the Fire: an eye that lowered itself from Allah's prohibitions, an eye that kept guard in the path of Allah, and an eye from which flowed like the head of a fly out of fear of Allah."
"8576","8571 - Ishaq ibn Jibril al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Abi Hisham informed us, from Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Aswad, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My ummah has been given in Ramadan five traits no ummah before them was given: the breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk; the angels seek forgiveness for them until they break their fast; the devils are chained therein and cannot reach therein what they used to reach in other than it; then He, blessed and exalted, says: My righteous servants are about to cast off from themselves hardship and harm - I think he said - and it passes to them, or they pass to their reward in the last night. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, is it Laylat al-Qadr? He said: No, but the worker is paid his wage when he completes his work. And we do not know this hadith reported from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except through this route with this chain, and Hisham ibn Abi Hisham is a man of Basra called Hisham ibn Ziyad Abu al-Miqdam; a group of scholars narrated from him, and he is not strong in hadith."
"8577","8572 - And Rawh ibn Hatim Abu Ghassan and Isma'il ibn Abi Isma'il narrated to us, they said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Zayd, he said: I said to Ayyub: Did you memorize anything like al-Hasan's saying about 'your affair is in your hand'? He said: No. Then he said: I seek Allah's forgiveness. Qatadah narrated it to me, from Kathir ibn Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurairah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), like al-Hasan's saying, and al-Hasan used to say: It is three. And we do not know this hadith reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this route with this chain, and Qatadah was not followed on this hadith; those below Qatadah are trustworthy - Ayyub, Hammad, and Sulayman ibn Harb - and the hadith is treated with caution despite this narration."
"8578","Zurarah ibn Mus'ab, from Abu Salamah. 8573 - Ahmad ibn al-Hakam ibn Zibyan al-Mazini and Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Haddadi narrated to us, they said: Musa ibn Mas'ud narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr al-Mulayki narrated to us, from Zurarah ibn Mus'ab, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites Ayat al-Kursi and the beginning of Ha-Mim, the Believer, is protected that day from every evil. And we do not know this hadith reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except through this route with this chain."
"8579","8574 - Abu Kinanah Muhammad ibn Ashras al-Mu'addib narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, he said: Hilal ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Hanafi narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Maymunah, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah and Abu Dharr, they said: A door of knowledge that a man learns is dearer to me than a thousand voluntary rak'ahs, and they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When death comes - or a wording like it - to a seeker of knowledge while he is in this state, he dies as a martyr. And we do not know anyone who narrated this statement from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Abu Hurairah and Abu Dharr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this chain."
"8580","8575 - And Abdullah ibn al-Sabbah narrated it to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, he said: Hilal ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Maymunah, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah and Abu Dharr, something similar. And Hilal ibn Abd al-Rahman is Basran, and Ata ibn Abi Maymunah is Basran; Shu'bah and others narrated from him, and there is Qadariyyah in him; Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated from him, and he is truthful."
"8581","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Abu Salamah. 8576 - al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When a judge judges and strives and is correct, he has two rewards, and if he judges and strives and errs, he has one reward. And we do not know for this hadith a chain from Abu Hurairah better than this chain, and we do not know anyone who shared with Abd al-Razzaq in this narration with this chain."
"8582","Muhajir, from Abu Salamah. 8577 - Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Qattan al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Rushayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, he said: Thawr ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Muhajir ibn Habib, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you travel, let the most reciting among you lead you, even if he is the youngest among you, and when he leads you, he is your commander. And this hadith with this wording we do not know reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from the narration of Abu Hurairah with this chain; Abu Hurairah and others narrated some of these words, but with this wording, no. And Muhajir ibn Habib narrated from Abu Salamah nothing but this hadith."
"8583","Al-A'raj, from Abu Salamah. 8578 - Rizqullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud al-Hafari narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The prophets are brothers from co-wives; their mothers are different, and their father is one."
"8584","Abu Hazim, from Abu Salamah. 8579 - Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Iyad Abu Damrah narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, he said: I know it only from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Disputation about the Quran is disbelief; the Quran was revealed in seven modes, so what you know, act upon it, and what you do not know, refer it to its scholar. And we do not know of Abu Hazim narrating a musnad report from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, except this hadith, and none narrated it but Abu Damrah."
"8585","Abd al-Majid ibn Suhayl, from Abu Salamah. 8580 - Sa'id ibn Bahr al-Qaratisisi and Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Razi narrated to us, they said: Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Hind, from Abd al-Majid ibn Suhayl, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My pulpit is upon a streamlet from the streamlets of Paradise."
"8586","Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Salamah. 8581 - Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah al-Dashtaki narrated to us, from Abu Ja'far, meaning al-Razi, from Husayn, meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, the punishment of the Fire, the trial of life and death, and the trial of the False Messiah, the Dajjal."
"8587","Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abu Salamah. 8582 - Muhammad ibn Miskin ibn Numaylah narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A previously-married woman is not married until she is consulted, and a virgin is not married until her permission is sought. They said: And how is her permission? He said: Silence."
"8588","8583 - And Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A virgin is not married until her permission is sought, and a previously-married woman is not married until she is consulted. It was said: And what is the virgin's permission? He said: Her silence."
"8589","8584 - Bishr ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to say in prayer over the dead: O Allah, forgive our living and our dead, our present and our absent, our young and our old, our males and our females. O Allah, whoever of us You keep alive, keep him alive upon Islam, and whoever of us You cause to die, cause him to die upon faith. And this hadith has been differed over from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir: al-Awza'i narrated it from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah; Ikrimah narrated it from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah; and Hammam narrated it from Yahya, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"8590","8585 - Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated qunut for a month, saying: O Allah, save al-Walid ibn al-Walid, Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi'ah, and Salamah ibn Hisham. O Allah, save the oppressed among the believers."
"8591","8586 - Muhammad ibn Miskin ibn Numaylah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Musa met Adam, peace be upon them, and said: You are Adam who expelled people from Paradise. Adam said to him: You are Musa whom Allah chose with His messengership and His speech, so how do you blame me for an act Allah decreed for me before He created me! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So Adam overcame Musa in argument."
"8592","8587 - And Bishr ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut in the last Isha prayer after bowing. And this wording we do not recall reported except from Abu Hurairah with this chain."
"8593","8588 - Bishr ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated in 'When the sky splits asunder.'"
"8594","8589 - Bishr ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts Ramadan with faith and seeking reward is forgiven his past sins, and whoever stands Laylat al-Qadr with faith and seeking reward is forgiven his past sins."
"8595","8590 - al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah and Bishr ibn Khalid narrated to us, with Bishr's wording, they said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: My close friend advised me with three: the two rak'ahs of Duha, not to sleep except upon witr, and fasting three days of every month. And we do not know anyone who narrated this from al-Awza'i except Muhammad ibn Kathir, and it is not reported from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, except through this route."
"8596","8591 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever keeps a dog, a qirat of his deeds decreases every day, except a dog for tilling or livestock."
"8597","8592 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade dubba' and muzaffat (vessels)."
"8598","8593 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: When the caller calls, Satan turns away passing wind; when the call ends, he returns; when the iqamah is made, he turns away; when it ends, he returns, until he comes between a man and himself, saying: Remember such-and-such and such-and-such, things he had not remembered, until he does not know whether he prayed three or four. So if he does not know whether he prayed three or four, let him prostrate two prostrations while sitting."
"8599","8594 - Bishr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), something similar."
"8600","8595 - And Bishr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The best day on which the sun has risen is Friday; on it Allah created Adam, on it He settled him in Paradise, on it he came out of it, and on it the Hour will come."
"8601","8596 - Bishr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not precede the month, meaning by a day or two days, except a day one of you used to fast, then let him fast it."
"8602","8597 - Bishr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say takbir whenever he lowered and raised himself."
"8603","8598 - Abdah ibn Abdullah and Ja'far ibn Mukram narrated to us, they said: al-Hafari narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought food at Marr al-Zahran, and said to Abu Bakr and Umar: Come near and eat. They said: We are fasting. He said: Work for your two companions; move on for your two companions. And we do not know anyone who narrated this from al-Awza'i except al-Thawri, nor from al-Thawri except Abu Dawud al-Hafari."
"8604","8599 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of one who comes early to Friday is like one who offers a camel, then the one after him like one who offers a cow, then the one after him like one who offers a sheep; when the imam sits on the pulpit, the scrolls are folded and they sit listening."
"8605","8600 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek refuge in Allah from the punishment of the grave and the punishment of the Fire, from the trial of life and death, and from the evil of the False Messiah, the Dajjal."
"8606","8601 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a sermon, and a man called Abu Shah stood and said: Write it for me, or write it down. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Write it for Abu Shah."
"8607","8602 - al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah ibn al-Bazzar al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not call grapes karm. And I have not memorized this hadith except from al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah; thus I found it in my book."
"8608","8603 - And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the first for whom the earth will split open on the Day of Resurrection."
"8609","8604 - And al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughirah Abd al-Quddus ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted, feels jealousy, and the believer feels jealousy, and Allah's jealousy is that the believer commits what Allah has forbidden him."
"8610","8605 - And Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah and Muhammad ibn al-Layth narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Musa, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, blessed and exalted, feels jealousy, and the believer feels jealousy, and Allah's jealousy is that the believer commits what Allah has forbidden him."
"8611","8606 - Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Sijistani narrated to us, he said: Abu Hafs al-Tinnisi Amr ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah, meaning Ibn Abdullah, narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My provision has been placed under the shade of my spear, humiliation and disgrace have been placed upon whoever opposes my command, and whoever imitates a people is one of them. And Sadaqah has been opposed in its chain: others narrated it from al-Awza'i with a different, mursal chain, and Sadaqah was not followed in this narration from al-Awza'i with this chain."
"8612","8607 - Yusuf ibn Musa and Muhammad ibn Hashim narrated to us, they said: al-Hasan ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: al-Mu'afa ibn Imran narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade every carnivore with fangs, and domestic donkeys - I think he said - and mujaththamah, khulsah, and nuhbah, and said: Whoever eats of this tree, let him not approach us in our mosque. And we do not recall this hadith from the hadith of al-Awza'i, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, except from the hadith of al-Mu'afa from him."
"8613","8608 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Sa'd ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Yazid narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you enters the mosque, let him not sit until he prays two rak'ahs. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Awza'i except Ibrahim ibn Yazid, and we do not know anyone who followed him in it."
"8614","8609 - Sa'dan ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak, meaning al-Suri, narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has never permitted anything as His permission for a prophet chanting the Quran aloud."
"8615","8610 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Juwayriyah narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, when were you recorded as a prophet? He said: While Adam was between the spirit and the body. Thus Abbad narrated it from al-Awza'i; others among al-Walid's companions also narrated it from al-Awza'i, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, and some of al-Walid's companions gave it a full chain from al-Awza'i, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"8616","8611 - al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah ibn al-Bazzar and Harun ibn Sufyan narrated to us, they said: Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr al-Raqqi narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah and Abu Sa'id mentioning from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: In Friday there is an hour no servant coincides with while praying, asking Allah therein for anything, but He gives it to him. He said: Abdullah ibn Salam said: It is the last hour. I said: He only said 'while praying,' and that is not a time of prayer. He said: Did you not hear, or has it not reached you, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever waits for prayer is in prayer?! And we do not know anyone who narrated this from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah and Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except Ma'mar."
"8617","8612 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurairah, he said: It was forbidden to hasten before Ramadan by a day or two days."
"8618","8613 - And al-Mundhir ibn al-Walid al-Jarudi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far, from Ayyub, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - counting these pebbles, pebbles in his hand - saying: Perform ablution because of what fire has touched. And we do not know anyone who narrated this from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, except al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far, and we heard it only from al-Jarudi, from his father."
"8619","8614 - And al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated it to us, Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), something similar."
"8620","8615 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A believer's dream is one part of forty-six parts of prophethood. And this hadith has been narrated from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, by Ali ibn al-Mubarak and by Ibn Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from his father."
"8621","8616 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever catches a rak'ah of the dawn prayer before the sun rises has caught it, and whoever catches a rak'ah of the Asr prayer before the sun sets has caught it."
"8622","8617 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The People of the Book used to read the Book in Hebrew and explain it in Arabic to the people of Islam, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not believe the People of the Book nor disbelieve them, and say: We believe in what was revealed to us and revealed to you. And we do not know this hadith reported from Abu Hurairah except through this route, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, except Ali ibn al-Mubarak."
"8623","8618 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man says to his brother: O disbeliever, one of them has incurred it. And we do not know this hadith reported from Abu Hurairah except through this route, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Yahya except Ali ibn al-Mubarak."
"8624","8619 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I hope that whoever witnessed Badr will not enter the Fire, if Allah wills. And we do not know this hadith reported from Abu Hurairah except through this route with this chain."
"8625","8620 - I found in my book in my handwriting: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the imam says 'Not of those who earned anger nor of the astray,' say: Amin, and when he says: Allah hears whoever praises Him, say: O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise."
"8626","8621 - al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Qadim narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Furafisah, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is naive and generous, and the wicked is cunning and mean. And we do not know this hadith reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this narration from Abu Hurairah; al-Hajjaj ibn Furafisah was followed by Bishr ibn Rafi', who narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"8627","8622 - Salamah narrated it to us - as far as I know - he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Bishr informed us; and Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Rafi' informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is naive and generous, and the wicked is cunning and mean."
"8628","8623 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Utbah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought forgiveness for the first row three times, for the second twice, and for the third once. And others narrated this hadith from Yahya disagreeing with Ayyub in his narration: Hisham narrated it from Yahya, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from al-Irbad; Shayban narrated it from Yahya, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from al-Irbad, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And the hadith of al-Irbad is from the hadith of Ayyub ibn Utbah, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah."
"8629","8624 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Utbah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three traits, whoever has them is a hypocrite even if he fasts, prays, and claims to be a believer: when he speaks he lies, when entrusted he betrays, and when he promises he breaks his promise. And this hadith has been reported from Abu Hurairah through other routes, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, except Ayyub ibn Utbah."
"8630","8625 - Muhammad ibn al-Layth Abu al-Sabbah al-Haddadi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Utbah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered killing the two black ones in prayer. And I fear Ayyub ibn Utbah erred in its chain when he narrated it from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah; the precise narrators narrate it from Yahya, from Damdam ibn Jaws, from Abu Hurairah."
"8631","8626 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Suwayd al-Yamami narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Four things in my ummah they will not abandon: boasting of lineages, disparaging ancestries, and wailing - the wailing woman will be raised on the Day of Resurrection, if she did not repent, wearing a garment of tar. And this hadith has been reported from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir with a different chain; Suwayd is not strong, and this is not preserved from the hadith of Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, except from the hadith of Suwayd, and he was not followed in it."
"8632","8627 - al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Abi Khath'am narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Wine is from these two trees, meaning dates and grapes. And this hadith is reported from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Kathir, from Abu Hurairah."
"8633","8628 - Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Sijistani narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Ibn Zahr, meaning Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, narrated to me, from Abu al-Munib, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: When one of you goes to his wife, let him cover himself; if he does not cover himself, the angels are shy and leave, and Satan remains, and if there is a child between them, Satan has a share in him. And we do not know this hadith reported with this wording from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain from Abu Hurairah from him, and its chain is not strong."
"8634","8629 - Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Khath'am narrated to me, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah: that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about wiping over the khuffs, and he said: For the resident, a day and a night, and for the traveler, three days and their nights. And Umar ibn Abdullah narrated from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Hurairah, hadiths he was not followed in, this among them; he also narrated, among what he was not followed in, what Abu Kurayb narrated: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Abi Khath'am narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays six rak'ahs after Maghrib."
"8635","8630 - Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Awn narrated to us, he said: Umar, meaning Ibn Abi Khath'am, narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you send a man to me, send one with a handsome face and a good name. And we do not know this hadith reported from Abu Hurairah except through this route, and we have already mentioned Umar's weakness."
"8636","8631 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Rashid informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One religion does not inherit from another. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, except Umar ibn Rashid, and he is lenient in hadith; and we do not know this wording reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this route, so we mentioned it despite its weak chain."
"8637","8631 (m) - Umar ibn Yunus mentioned, he said: Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman is not married over her paternal aunt nor over her maternal aunt."
"8638","8632 - al-Hasan ibn Sa'id al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Ghassan ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not accept charity from misappropriated spoils nor prayer without purification. And we do not know this hadith reported from Abu Hurairah except through this route with this chain, and al-Hakam ibn Musa also narrated this hadith from Ghassan ibn Ubayd."
"8639","8633 - Isma'il ibn Mas'ud narrated to us, he said: al-Mu'tamir narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Amir narrating from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah: that the Jews used to say that coitus interruptus is the lesser burying alive of daughters, and it reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: The Jews have lied; when Allah wills to create a creature, nothing prevents Him - I think he said - nothing. And we do not know anyone who narrated this from Yahya except Abu Amir."
"8640","8634 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Aban ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Yamami narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am so-and-so, daughter of so-and-so. He said: Say what your need is. She said: My need is that so-and-so is proposing to me, so tell me what is the husband's right over the wife; if it is something I can bear, I will marry him, and if I cannot, I will not marry. He said: Among the husband's rights over the wife is that if his nostrils flowed with blood and pus and she licked it, she would not have fulfilled his right; and if it were fitting for a human to prostrate to a human, I would have ordered the woman to prostrate to her husband when he comes to her. She said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I will never marry as long as I remain in this world."
"8641","8635 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three traits, whoever has them, Allah will reckon him an easy reckoning and admit him to Paradise by His mercy. They said: And what are they, O Prophet of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you? He said: You give to whoever deprived you, you join with whoever cut you off, and you pardon whoever wronged you; when you do that, He will admit you to Paradise by His mercy."
"8642","8636 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Yamami narrated to us - he is known as Sulayman ibn Abi Sulayman; Umar ibn Yunus, Sa'id ibn Sulayman Sa'dawayh, and al-Qasim ibn al-Hakam narrated from him - Ahmad narrated to us from al-Qasim ibn al-Hakam, from Sulayman ibn Dawud, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: By the One who sent me with the truth, this world will not end until collapse, pelting, and transformation befall them. They said: And when is that, O Prophet of Allah? He said: When you see women riding saddles, singing girls increase, false testimony spreads, and men suffice themselves with men and women with women."
"8643","8637 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, he said: Sulayman narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked Abu Bakr: How do you perform witr? He said: I perform witr at the beginning of the night. He said: Cautious and shrewd. Then he asked Umar: How do you perform witr? He said: At the end of the night. He said: Strong and aided."
"8644","8638 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever comes to this House from unlawful earnings, proceeding in other than Allah's obedience, when he enters ihram and places his foot in the stirrup or saddle, and his mount sets off with him, saying: Labbayk, O Allah, labbayk, a caller from heaven calls him: No labbayk for you and no blessed response; your earnings are unlawful, your provision is unlawful, your mount is unlawful, so return burdened with sin, not rewarded, and expect what displeases you. And when a man goes out for hajj with lawful wealth, places his foot in the stirrup, and his mount sets off with him, saying: Labbayk, O Allah, labbayk, a caller from heaven calls him: Labbayk and blessed response, I have answered you; your mount is lawful, your clothes are lawful, your provision is lawful, so return rewarded, not burdened, and expect what pleases you."
"8645","8639 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever builds for Allah a house in which Allah is worshipped, from lawful wealth, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise. And the hadiths of Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Yamami we do not know anyone who shared them from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, and in my view he is not strong, for his hadiths indicate that, if Allah wills."
"8646","8640 - Sahl ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Sadaqah ibn Yazid, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: People pointed at a crescent one night and said: How beautiful it is? How clear it is? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How will you be when you are from your Lord like the moon on the night of full moon, none of you perceives Him except the perceptive. And we do not know this hadith reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this route with this chain."
"8647","Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah. 8641 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Quraysh, the Ansar, Aslam, Ghifar, Muzaynah, and Ashja' are my allies; they have no ally besides Allah and His Messenger. Thus Shu'bah narrated it from Sa'd, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah; al-Mas'udi narrated it from Sa'd, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurairah; and Sa'd ibn Amr ibn Sa'id narrated it from Sa'd, from Abu Salamah, from his father."
"8648","8642 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: While a man was riding a cow, it turned and said: I was not created for this; I was created for plowing. He said: I believe in it, I and Abu Bakr and Umar. He said: And a wolf seized a sheep and the shepherd followed it, and the wolf said: Who is for it on the day of beasts, a day when it has no shepherd but me. Then he said: I believe in it, I and Abu Bakr and Umar. Abu Salamah said: And they were not then among the people."
"8649","8643 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr two rak'ahs then gave salam, and one of the people asked him: Has the prayer been shortened? - I think he said - then he prayed two rak'ahs, gave salam, then prostrated two prostrations."
"8650","8644 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sa'd, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Come to prayer with calmness and dignity upon you; pray what you catch and make up what you missed."
"8651","8645 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Bazi' narrated to us, he said: Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the delegation of Abd al-Qays - I think - from dubba', hantam, and naqir. And we do not know anyone who narrated this from Shu'bah, from Sa'd, except Abu Bahr; more than one narrated it to us from Abu Bahr."
"8652","Abu al-Zinad, from Abu Salamah. 8646 - Firdaws al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Mahdi ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A cat does not cut off prayer; it is only among the furnishings of the house."
"8653","8647 - And Abu Ghassan narrated it to us, he said: Mahdi narrated to us, from Ibn Abi al-Zinad, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A cat is among the furnishings of the house."
"8654","Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay' . 8648 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Awn said: Hafs ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My ummah will remain upon fitrah as long as they pray Fajr at dawn brightness. And this statement is not reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this route with this chain; Abd al-Aziz narrated from Abu Salamah nothing but this hadith, and Hafs is lenient in hadith, narrating rejected hadiths, but since we only recall this hadith from his hadith, we mentioned it from him and clarified its defect."
"8655","Makhul, from Abu Salamah. 8649 - Muhammad ibn Abi Ghalib narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Walid narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit, from his father, from al-Zuhri and Makhul, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man's prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer alone by twenty-five parts. And we do not know of Makhul narrating from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, except this hadith."
"8656","Al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Salamah. 8650 - Isa ibn Musa al-Sami narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Harith, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: If he drinks wine, flog him; then if he drinks it, flog him; then if he drinks, flog him; then if he drinks, kill him. And Umar ibn Abi Salamah narrated this hadith from Ibn Abbas, from Abu Hurairah, with a like narration as well."
"8657","8651 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, they said: Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from his maternal uncle al-Harith, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: Every soul has its share of zina decreed for it. And Yahya abridged this hadith; others narrated it at length, mentioning therein: Every soul has its share of zina decreed for it; the zina of the eye is looking, the zina of the hand is seizing, the zina of the leg is walking, and the private part confirms that or denies it."
"8658","Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Abu Salamah. 8652 - Mu'adh ibn Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The truest word a poet said: And Sharik narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the pulpit and said that upon the pulpit."
"8659","8653 - Amr ibn Ali, Muhammad ibn Bashshar, Muhammad ibn Ma'mar, and al-Sakan ibn Sa'id narrated to us, they said: Mu'ammal narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to his companions while they were in the mosque in circles, and said: Why do I see you in separate groups. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abd al-Malik, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, except Mu'ammal from al-Thawri, and he was not followed in it."
"8660","8654 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The one consulted is entrusted. And the narration of this hadith from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr has been differed over; thus Shayban said from Abd al-Malik, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah."
"8661","Qatadah from Abu Salamah. 8655 - Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Kabir narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Asim narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts Ramadan with faith and seeking reward is forgiven his past sins. From the hadith of Abdullah ibn Abi Labid, from Abu Salamah."
"8662","8656 - Abu al-Sabbah Muhammad ibn al-Layth narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ibn Abi Labid, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There was a prophet among the prophets who used to draw lines, so whoever coincides with his line, that or whoever coincides with that line, knows. And we do not know anyone who narrated this from Ibn Abi Labid, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, except Sufyan; Ibn Abi Labid narrated from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the story of Dhu al-Yadayn, which Ibn Uyaynah narrated from him."
"8663","Imran ibn Abi Anas from Abu Salamah. 8657 - Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us, he said: Shabab ibn Sawwar narrated to us, he said: al-Layth informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Imran ibn Abi Anas, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed and gave salam after two rak'ahs, and Dhu al-Shimalayn caught up with him and said: O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been shortened or did you forget? He said: It was neither shortened nor did I forget. He said: Yes, by the One who sent you with the truth. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is it as Dhu al-Yadayn says? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. So he prayed two rak'ahs with the people."
"8664","Amr ibn Dinar from Abu Salamah. 8658 - Azhar ibn Jamil narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adiyy narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A woman is not married over her paternal aunt nor over her maternal aunt. Thus Ibn Adiyy said from Shu'bah; more than one shortened it, narrating it from Amr, from Abu Salamah, mursal."
"8665","8659 - Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Rawh narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Hafsa narrated to us, from Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah has never permitted anything as His permission for a prophet chanting the Quran - or a wording like it. And al-Zuhri gave this hadith a full chain from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah; we do not know anyone who gave it a full chain from Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, except Ibn Abi Hafsa, and nothing is preserved from Ibn Abi Hafsa, from Amr, but this hadith."
"8666","Umar ibn Abi Salamah from his father from Abu Hurairah. 8660 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: al-Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade muhaqalah and muzabanah; muzabanah is selling palm trees for dates, and muhaqalah is selling wheat for standing crop."
"8667","8661 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Disputation about the Quran is disbelief."
"8668","8662 - And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated it to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), something similar."
"8669","8663 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A believer's soul remains suspended as long as there is a debt upon him. Thus Sufyan said from Sa'd, from Amr ibn Abi Salamah, without saying: from his father."
"8670","8664 - And Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A believer's soul remains suspended by his debt until his debt is paid off."
"8671","8665 - Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you cleans himself with stones, let him use an odd number."
"8672","8666 - Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed women who visit graves."
"8673","8667 - Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When a slave steals, sell him even for a worthless rope."
"8674","8668 - Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman and her paternal aunt are not combined in marriage, nor a woman and her maternal aunt."
"8675","8669 - And Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Three things, each is a duty upon every Muslim: visiting the sick, attending funerals, and saying yarhamukallah to a sneezer when he praises Allah."
"8676","8670 - And Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you strikes, let him avoid the face."
"8677","8671 - Talut ibn Abbad narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah. Thus Talut said."
"8678","8672 - And Abu Kamil narrated it to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give charity, for I intend to send an expedition. Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have four thousand; two thousand I lend to my Lord and two thousand for my dependents. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah bless for you what you gave and bless for you what you kept. And a man of the Ansar spent the night and earned two sa's of dates, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I earned two sa's of dates; one sa' I lend to my Lord and one sa' for my dependents. The hypocrites sneered at him and said: The one Ibn Awf gave, he gave only for show; and they said: Was Allah and His Messenger not in need of this one's sa'? So Allah, blessed and exalted, revealed: 'Those who criticize the contributors among the believers in charities and those who find nothing but their effort,' to the end of the verse. And we do not know this hadith reported from Abu Hurairah except through this route, and we have not heard anyone giving it a full chain from the hadith of Umar ibn Abi Salamah except Talut from Abu Awanah."
"8679","8673 - Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the briber and the bribed in judgment. And Amr narrated this hadith from his father, from Abu Hurairah; al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated it from Abu Salamah, from Abdullah ibn Amr. And the nephew of Abu Salamah narrated it from his uncle, from his father."
"8680","8674 - Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was given comprehensive speech, aided with awe, while I was sleeping I was brought the keys of the earth's treasures and they were placed in my hand, I was sent to all people, spoils were made lawful for me, and the prophets were sealed with me."
"8681","8675 - And Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let the beards grow, and trim the mustaches."
"8682","8676 - And Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you hears the iqamah, let him come with calmness upon him; let him pray what he catches and make up what he missed."
"8683","8677 - Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are days of eating, meaning the days of tashriq."
"8684","8678 - Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever seizes a handspan of land will be collared with it - or with her - from seven earths."
"8685","8679 - And with its chain, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no omen except your omen. Three times."
"8686","8680 - Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, I am Your servant and Your Messenger, and I have sanctified what is between its two lava plains as Ibrahim sanctified Makkah."
"8687","8681 - Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Change white hair, and do not resemble the Jews."
"8688","8682 - al-Hasan ibn Mudrik narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man of the Children of Israel used to lend people money; a man came to him and said: O so-and-so, lend me six hundred dinars. He said: Yes; where is your guarantor? He said: Allah is my guarantor. He said: Yes. So he counted out six hundred dinars for him, set a term, and the other rode the sea with the wealth trading with it. Allah decreed that the term came and the other did not arrive, and the sea rose between them. The owner of the wealth went to the shore to ask about him, and those he asked about him said: We left him in such-and-such village. The owner of the wealth said: O Allah, I only gave it for You. He said: And the one who owed the wealth went and hollowed a piece of wood when the term fell due, placed the wealth inside it, wrote a note to him: From so-and-so to so-and-so, I have paid your wealth to my guarantor who stood surety for me. Then he fastened the mouth of the wood and cast it into the sea. The sea carried it until it cast it onto the shore. The owner of the wealth went asking about his companion as he used to ask, and found the wood and carried it to his family; he said: Burn this. The dinars and the note scattered from it; he read it and recognized. And it was decreed for the other, and he came afterwards and the owner of the wealth came to him and said: O so-and-so, the wait has been long. He said: Yes. He said: As for me, I paid it to my guarantor who stood surety for me; as for you, here is your wealth, take it. He said: Your guarantor has already paid me. Abu Hurairah said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and our chatter and voices grew loud about which of them was more trustworthy. And we do not know this hadith reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this route with this chain."
"8689","8683 - Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes to prayer, let him come with calmness upon him; what he catches, let him pray, and what he missed, let him complete."
"8690","8684 - Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will keep asking until one of them says: This was created, so who created Allah?"
"8691","8685 - Khalid narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that when morning came he used to say: We have entered morning and the dominion belongs to Allah, praise belongs to Allah, there is no partner for Him, there is no god but Allah, and to Him is the resurrection; and when evening came he said: We have entered evening and the evening dominion and all praise belongs to Allah, there is no partner for Him, there is no god but Him, and to Him is the return."
"8692","8686 - Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I asked my Lord for three things; He gave me two and withheld one from me: I asked my Lord not to destroy my ummah by famine, and He did; I asked my Lord not to destroy my ummah, some by others, and He withheld it from me; and I asked Him not to set over them an enemy from besides them, and He did."
"8693","8687 - Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prays and does not know whether he prayed two or three, let him prostrate two prostrations while sitting."
"8694","8688 - Khalid narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Time draws near, knowledge is taken away, trials appear, and harj increases. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and what is harj? He said: Killing."
"8695","8689 - Khalid narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On the night I was taken, I passed - and he described the prophets - and I placed my hand where the prophets' feet are placed of Bayt al-Maqdis; I passed by Isa son of Maryam, and the nearest people to him in resemblance is Urwah ibn Mas'ud; and Musa is curly-haired, lean among men, as if from the men of Shanu'ah; and Ibrahim was shown to me, peace be upon him, and the nearest people to him in resemblance is your companion, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"8696","8690 - Khalid narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The major sins, the first of them: associating with Allah, killing a soul without its right, consuming riba, consuming an orphan's wealth, fleeing on the day of battle, slandering chaste women, and returning to the bedouins after emigration."
"8697","8691 - And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah feels jealousy, and the believer feels jealousy, and Allah's jealousy is that His servant commits what He has forbidden him."
"8698","Al-Hasan ibn Yazid al-Damri, from Abu Salamah. 8692 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Yazid, he said: I heard Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrating from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant or maidservant swears at this pulpit - I think he said - a false oath, even for a moist siwak, but the Fire becomes due for him."
"8699","8693 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see it, meaning the crescent of Ramadan, fast, and when you see it, meaning the crescent of Shawwal, break your fast."
"8700","8694 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ziyad, from Hilal ibn Usamah, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Surplus water is not withheld to withhold thereby pasture. And we do not know of Hilal narrating a musnad report from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, except this hadith."
"8701","Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Yazid ibn Abd al-Malik al-Nawfali narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from my grandfather, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Six mudds suffice for the ghusl of janabah."" This hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Abu Salamah except Abd al-Malik Abu Yazid, and he is not strong in hadith, and the hadith is not known to be narrated except through this route with this chain."
"8702","Abdullah ibn Fayruz ibn al-Danaj. Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from Abdullah al-Danaj, he said: I heard Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, in the time of Khalid ibn Abdullah al-Qasri, in this mosque, the mosque of Kufah, and al-Hasan came and sat with him, and he narrated, he said: Abu Hurayrah narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The sun and the moon are two bulls in the Fire on the Day of Resurrection."" Al-Hasan said to him: And what is their sin? Al-Hasan said to him: I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and you say, I think he said: and what is their sin? This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayrah except through this route with this chain, and we do not know of Abdullah al-Danaj narrating from Abu Salamah except this hadith."
"8703","Salamah ibn Kuhayl. Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""The best of you are the best of you in repayment."""
"8704","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: I think Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, from Shubah, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. This hadith was narrated from Salamah by more than one; among them Shubah and al-Thawri and Ali ibn Salih and others, and there is more discussion about it than this."
"8705","Said ibn al-Harith, from Abu Salamah. Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ayan narrated to us, he said: Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Harith, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, I think he raised it, that he used to say: There is an hour on Friday which no believing man coincides with, asking Allah for good therein, except He gives it to him, while he is in prayer, making it brief. He said: When Abu Hurayrah died I blamed myself for not having asked him about it, then I said: Here is Abu Said al-Khudri, and he is older in companionship to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); perhaps I will find with him knowledge from the Messenger of Allah. So I entered upon Abu Said and I found him, I think, with date-stalk clusters before him. I said: What are these clusters, O Abu Said? He said: These are clusters in which Allah has placed blessing for us; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lean on one, so we cut a stalk for him, and while it was in his hand he saw spittle in the mosque, so he scraped it off with it, then he turned to the people and said: ""O people, when one of you is in prayer, let him not spit in front of him; let him spit to his left or under his feet, and if he does not find a spittoon, I think he said, then in his sandal or in his garment."" He said: The sky stirred that day, and it coincided. A flash lightning shone in a dark night, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, I knew that those attending the prayer were few, so I wanted to attend it with you. He said: ""Remain firm; when you pray..."" When, I think he said, he prayed, he passed by him and raised the stalk to him and said: ""Go out with it; when you see a dark figure in your house, strike it with it, for it is a devil."" So he did. He said: I said: O Abu Said, the hour that is on Friday? He said: We asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about it. He said: I had, I think he said, known it, then I was made to forget it. He said: So I left him until I came to the house of a man from the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I said: This is a man who has read the Torah and accompanied the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So I entered upon him and said: Inform me about this hour which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to speak of on Friday. He said: Yes; Allah created Adam on Friday, and settled him in Paradise on Friday, and sent him down to earth on Friday, and took his soul on Friday, and it is the day on which the Hour will come, and it is the last hour of Friday. He said: I said: Do you not know that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says: while in prayer? He said: Do you not know that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever waits for a prayer is in prayer."" We do not know of Said ibn al-Harith narrating from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, except this hadith, and the hadith has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah through other routes."
"8706","Nuaym al-Mujmir, from Abu Salamah. Ismail ibn Yaqub al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa ibn Ayan narrated to me, he said: my father narrated to me, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from Nuaym al-Mujmir, he said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to prostrate in ""When the sky splits asunder."" This hadith has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah through various routes, and we do not know of Nuaym al-Mujmir narrating from Abu Salamah except this hadith."
"8707","Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari, from Abu Salamah. Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever fasts Ramadan with faith and seeking reward, his past sins are forgiven."" This hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, except Ibn Fudayl."
"8708","I found in my book, in my handwriting, from Abu Bakr ibn Khallad, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Take sahur, for in sahur there is blessing."" This hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Ibn Fudayl except Abu Bakr ibn Khallad, and he was not followed in it, and he mentioned that he heard it from him in Makkah."
"8709","Al-Miswar ibn Rifah, from Abu Salamah. Abu Bakr ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn al-Ala narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What is between my house and my minbar is a garden from the gardens of Paradise, and a prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere, except the Sacred Mosque."""
"8710","Abu Bakr ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn al-Ala narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Miswar ibn Rifah, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, with something similar. We do not know of al-Miswar ibn Rifah narrating from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, except this hadith."
"8711","Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah; Zayd ibn Aslam from Ata. Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Habib al-Raqqi informed us, he said: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Khaliq narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar and Busr ibn Said and Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Whoever catches a rakah of Asr before the sun sets has caught it, and whoever catches a rakah of Fajr before the sun rises has caught it."""
"8712","Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Busr ibn Said and Abd al-Rahman al-Araj and Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), something similar."
"8713","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Abu Ghassan, and he is Muhammad ibn Mutarrif, narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar to the hadith of Malik. Muhammad ibn Mutarrif, from Zayd ibn Aslam, did not mention Busr ibn Said nor Abd al-Rahman al-Araj. We do not know of Zayd ibn Aslam narrating from Busr ibn Said except this hadith."
"8714","Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn Askar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not make nabidh in dubba, nor in hantam, nor in muzaffat."" This hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Zayd, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, except Ibn Jurayj, and it is not narrated from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, except with this chain."
"8715","Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari and Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Saigh narrated to us, they said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the woman who joins hair and the woman who asks for it to be joined. This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayrah except through this route, and none narrated it from Zayd ibn Aslam except Fulayh ibn Sulayman."
"8716","Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ayan narrated to us, he said: Fulayh, meaning Ibn Sulayman, narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrating it from his Lord, Blessed and Exalted, He said: ""Fasting is Mine, and I reward for it; the breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk."" This hadith has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah through various routes, and it is not known to be narrated from the hadith of Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, except from the hadith of Fulayh from him."
"8717","Muhammad ibn Ghalib and Rawh ibn Hatim Abu Ghassan narrated to us, they said: Musa ibn Masud narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Husayn, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Paradise is one hundred degrees; between every two degrees is what is between heaven and earth."" This hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Ata ibn Yasar except Zayd ibn Aslam, nor from Zayd ibn Aslam except Ibn Abi Husayn, nor from Ibn Abi Husayn except Muhammad ibn Muslim."
"8718","Ali ibn Muslim, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan, and Abdah ibn Abdullah narrated to us, they said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mutarrif informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever goes in the morning or evening to the mosque, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, prepares for him a place of hospitality in Paradise, each time he goes in the morning or evening."" This hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Zayd, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, except Muhammad ibn Mutarrif, and he is a man from the people of Madinah, there is no harm in him."
"8719","Al-Fadl ibn Sahl and Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Saigh narrated to us, they said: al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: ""The tooth of the disbeliever is like Uhud, his thigh is like al-Bayda, and the thickness of his skin is forty-two cubits, by the cubit of the All-Compelling."" This hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, except Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Dinar, and it was narrated by more than one from Abd al-Rahman."
"8720","Al-Fadl ibn Sahl, Ahmad ibn Mansur, and Ibrahim ibn Ziyad narrated to us, they said: al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""There will be rulers over you who pray for you; if they get it right, it is for you and for them, and if they err, it is for you and against them."" This hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Zayd, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, except Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Dinar, and it was narrated from Abd al-Rahman by others than al-Hasan ibn Musa."
"8721","Abu Ghassan Rawh ibn Hatim, and he was among the understanding, trustworthy ones, narrated to us, he said: Qurrah ibn Habib narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is an hour on Friday which no Muslim coincides with, asking Allah for good, except He gives it to him."" The wording of this hadith and its like has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah through various routes, and it is not known to be narrated from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, except through this route, and none narrated it from Zayd ibn Aslam except Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Dinar."
"8722","Ali ibn Qurrah ibn Habib narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""We are the last, the foremost on the Day of Resurrection; they were given the Book before us and we were given it after them; they sought the day of Friday, and Allah guided us to it; people follow us: the Jews tomorrow, and the Christians the day after."" This hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, except Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Dinar, nor from Abd al-Rahman except Qurrah ibn Habib, and we heard it only from his son Ali, from his father. Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Dinar is sound in hadith; a group of people of knowledge narrated from him, among them al-Hasan ibn Musa and Hashim ibn al-Qasim and others, and he narrated hadiths from Zayd ibn Aslam and others which none but he narrated, and his hadith was accepted."
"8723","Ubayd ibn Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, or Zayd ibn Khalid, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs wudu and performs it well, then prays two rakahs in which he does not forget, is forgiven."" This hadith was narrated by others than Hisham, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Zayd ibn Khalid."
"8724","Muhammad ibn Amir al-Antaki narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Hunayni narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever spends a pair from his wealth, the keepers of Paradise call him: O servant of Allah, this is good; if he was among the people of prayer, he is called from the gate of prayer, and if he was among the people of charity, he is called from the gate of charity, and if he was among the people of fasting, he is called from the gate of al-Rayyan."" Abu Bakr said: No one called from any of these gates suffers any necessity; is anyone called from all of them? He said: ""Yes, and I hope you are among them; how excellent!"" This hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it except Hisham ibn Sad, nor from Hisham except al-Hunayni. Al-Hunayni was a man from the people of Madinah; he left it and traveled to the frontier, and his sight went, and he narrated hadiths from the people of Madinah which none but he narrated."
"8725","Mamar ibn Sahl narrated to us; al-Mualla ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Usamah ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from his father, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim; he does not wrong him and does not forsake him. All of the Muslim is forbidden to the Muslim: his blood and his wealth. Taqwa is here, and he pointed with his hand to his chest, saying it twice."" This hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, except Usamah, his son; and others than Usamah narrated it from Zayd, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah."
"8726","Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farwi narrated to us, he said: Usamah ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from his father, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Khalid ibn al-Walid is a sword from the swords of Allah."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayrah except through this route, and none narrated it from Zayd ibn Aslam with this chain except his son Usamah, nor from Usamah except Ishaq ibn Muhammad, and we heard it only from Abdullah ibn Shabib. It has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through various routes that he said: ""Khalid ibn al-Walid is a sword from the swords of Allah."""
"8727","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, they said: Ibrahim ibn Sulayman al-Dabbas narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever marries a woman for a dower while intending not to pay it to her is a fornicator, and whoever takes on a debt while intending not to pay it to its owner, I think he said, is a thief."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from the hadith of Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, except from the hadith of Muhammad ibn Aban. Muhammad ibn Aban is a man from the people of Kufah, and he is Ibn Aban ibn Salih; he was not a memorizer, and a group of eminent people narrated from him, among them Abu al-Walid and Abu Dawud and others."
"8728","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"8729","Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah ibn Yazid narrated it to us, he said: Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to combine the two prayers while traveling. This hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Zayd ibn Aslam except Muhammad ibn Aban, and our mention of Muhammad ibn Aban has already come in other than this hadith."
"8730","Abu al-Walid Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Walid ibn Muhammad ibn Burd narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sad, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Jibril (peace be upon him) came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Adha and said: How do you see this rite of ours? He said: ""The people of heaven are shown it with pride. Know, O Muhammad, that a young sheep is better than a noble goat, and know, O Muhammad, that a young sheep is better than a noble cow or camel; had Allah, Blessed and Exalted, known anything better than this, He would have ransomed Ibrahim (peace be upon him) with it."" This hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Hisham ibn Sad, from Zayd, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, except Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Hunayni, and none but him followed him with this narration; he brought hadiths he narrated which he was not followed in, because when his sight went and he went far from Madinah, moving to the frontier, he narrated hadiths from the people of Madinah, and some of them were rejected against him."
"8731","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A woman was forgiven who passed a dog panting over a well, so she took off her shoe and gave it water."" This hadith, its wording has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah through various routes, and we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, except Abdullah ibn Jafar. Abdullah ibn Jafar has had hadiths he narrated from the people of Madinah rejected against him, which none but he narrated; he was sound in hadith from the people of Madinah. A group narrated from him, among them Bishr ibn Muadh, Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam, Muhammad ibn al-Husayn, and others; only the hadith whose origin is known is written from his hadith, to show that he narrated this hadith through this route."
"8732","Sahl ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Salt Abu Yala narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about donkeys, whether anything had been revealed to him about them. He said: ""Nothing has been revealed to me about them except this single, comprehensive verse: 'Whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it.'"" This hadith was narrated by others than Ibn Uyaynah, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah; Suhayl narrated it from his father, from Abu Hurayrah; and Ibn Uyaynah narrated it from Ibn Ajlan, from Zayd."
"8733","Muhammad ibn Amr from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah. Al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Dharra narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Wadih narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Said, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""No fatigue, nor weariness, nor worry, nor grief befalls the believer, even a thorn he is pricked with or that pricks him, except Allah expiates thereby some of his sins."""
"8734","Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated it to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Said, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"8735","Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated it to us, he said: Said ibn Maslamah narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Said, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar to the hadith of Muhammad ibn Ishaq."
"8736","Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Sijistani and Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us, they said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Nafi ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Amr, meaning Ibn Ata, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The testimony of a Bedouin against a villager is not permitted."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated except from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, through this route with this chain; its chain is sound, and the hadith is not known from the Messenger of Allah except through this route."
"8737","Safwan ibn Sulaym from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah. Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Muttalib, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The fornicator does not fornicate while he is a believer when he fornicates, the thief does not steal while he is a believer, he does not drink wine while he is a believer when he drinks it, and he does not plunder a plunder of value while he is a believer when he plunders it."" This hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Safwan, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, except Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Muttalib; he is a man from the people of Madinah. The wording of this hadith has been narrated from the Messenger of Allah through various routes."
"8738","Zayd ibn Akhzam Abu Talib al-Tai narrated to us, he said: Yamar ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: al-Zubayr ibn Said narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A man speaks a word to make his companions laugh, falling thereby farther than al-Thurayya."" This hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Safwan, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, except al-Zubayr ibn Said, and we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Zubayr except Ibn al-Mubarak. Al-Zubayr ibn Said was narrated from by Ibn al-Mubarak and Jarir ibn Hazim, and he narrated several hadiths in which he was not followed, and this is among them."
"8739","Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Yahya ibn Hani narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has ninety-nine names; whoever enumerates them enters Paradise. Allah is Odd and loves the odd."" This hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Safwan, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, except Muhammad ibn Ishaq, nor from Muhammad except Yahya ibn Hani al-Shajari; his son Ibrahim narrated from him. It has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah through many routes."
"8740","Azhar ibn Jamil narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Zayd, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, raising it, he said: Recitation was made easy for Dawud (peace be upon him); he would order his mount to be saddled, and would not finish it until he completed the recitation. This hadith has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), through other than one route."
"8741","Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, he said: While a man was stealing, Isa (peace be upon him) looked at him. Isa said to him: Are you stealing? He said: By Allah, I did not do it. He said: I believe in Allah and disbelieve my sight. This hadith was narrated by Ibrahim ibn Tahman, saying: from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah; and it has been narrated from Hammam, from Abu Hurayrah."
"8742","What Amr ibn Dinar narrated from Ata. Tamim ibn al-Muntasir al-Wasiti, Ahmad ibn Sinan, and Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us, they said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, from Ayyub, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the obligatory one."" Yazid said: Hammad ibn Zayd also informed us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, and he did not raise it."
"8743","This hadith, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated it to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, as mawquf, with something similar. So narrated the companions of Hammad, from Hammad, with this chain, as mawquf. Abd al-Warith narrated it from Ayyub, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, as mawquf."
"8744","Ahmad ibn Malik al-Qasri narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, as mawquf. Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated it from Ayyub, as mawquf."
"8745","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, and he did not raise it. Mamar narrated it from Ayyub, from Amr ibn Dinar, as marfu."
"8746","Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from Ayyub, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, raising it, he said: ""When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the obligatory one."" Mamar was followed in raising it by what Yazid ibn Harun narrated, from Hammad ibn Zayd, from Ayyub, from Amr ibn Dinar, in the raising. Ibn Uyaynah narrated it but did not attach its chain from Amr."
"8747","Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated it to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the obligatory one. This hadith was raised from Amr, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, by Hammad ibn Zayd, from Ayyub, from Amr, and Mamar, from Ayyub, from Amr; and Warqa ibn Umar, al-Husayn ibn al-Muallim, Zakariyya ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn Juhadah, Hammad ibn Salamah, Muhammad ibn Muslim, and Ziyad ibn Sad. As for the hadith of Warqa:"
"8748","Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar, Amr ibn Ali, al-Walid ibn Sufyan al-Attar, and Ahmad ibn Thabit al-Jahdari narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Warqa, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the obligatory one."" We do not know of Shubah narrating from Warqa except two hadiths, this being one of them. As for the hadith of Muhammad ibn Juhadah from Amr:"
"8749","Amr ibn Ali and al-Hasan ibn Qazah narrated it to us, they said: Ziyad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the obligatory one."" We do not know of Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrating from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, except two hadiths, this being one of them, the other being disputed about from Amr ibn Dinar."
"8750","Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ayan narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out of the lavatory and food was brought to him, and it was said: Will you not perform wudu? Shall we not bring you water for wudu? He said: ""I do not intend prayer."" This hadith, I think Muhammad ibn Juhadah erred in its chain when he narrated it from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah; what is correct is what Amr ibn Dinar narrated, from Said ibn al-Huwayrith, from Ibn Abbas. So narrated Ayyub, Ibn Uyaynah, and a group, from Amr ibn Dinar. Husayn al-Muallim, Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Taifi, Ziyad ibn Sad, and Hammad ibn Salamah narrated from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the obligatory one."" As for the hadith of Husayn al-Muallim:"
"8751","Hilal ibn al-Ala narrated it to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Husayn al-Muallim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"8752","As for the hadith of Zakariyya ibn Ishaq: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So narrated Abd al-Ala, from Zakariyya, from Amr, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah. Abu Asim differed with him in its chain, narrating it from Zakariyya, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). What is correct is the hadith of Amr from Ata ibn Yasar. We do not know of al-Husayn al-Muallim narrating from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, except this hadith, nor did anyone narrate it from him except Isa ibn Yunus."
"8753","As for the hadith of Muhammad ibn Muslim: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim, the companion of al-Sabiri, narrated it to us, he said: Dawud ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"8754","As for the hadith of Hammad ibn Salamah: Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Haddadi narrated it to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the obligatory one."" This hadith was narrated by others than Muslim, from Hammad, from Amr, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, as mawquf. Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated it from Ziyad ibn Sad, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the obligatory one."" This hadith was narrated to us by one of our companions, and I did not mention him, since the one who narrated it to us is not one from whom this hadith should be mentioned; even if the hadith has an origin from Fudayl, more than one narrated it from him."
"8755","Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Ashath ibn Said narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""When a man goes bankrupt and a man finds his goods intact, he has more right to them."" In this hadith Ashath ibn Said erred, and he is lenient in hadith, when he narrated it from Amr, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah; what is correct is what Ibn Uyaynah narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Hisham ibn Yahya, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"8756","Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated it to us with it, he said: Ibn Uyaynah informed us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Hisham ibn Yahya, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ashath ibn Said Abu al-Rabi al-Samman is weak in hadith due to the abundance of errors in what he narrated, even though a group of those ascribed to knowledge narrated from him."
"8757","What Sharik ibn Abi Namir narrated from Ata. Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Sharik ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Namir, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: ""My servant does not draw near to Me with anything better than performing what I have made obligatory upon him, and My servant keeps drawing near to Me with supererogatory acts until I love him; when I love him, I am his hearing with which he hears, his sight with which he sees, and his hand with which he grasps. If he asks Me, I will give him; if he calls upon Me, I will answer him; if he seeks refuge in Me, I will grant him refuge. I do not hesitate about anything I do as I hesitate about the soul of the believer: he dislikes death, and I dislike his distress."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayrah except through this route with this chain. Umar ibn Ishaq ibn Yasar narrated it from his uncle Ata ibn Yasar, from Maymunah."
"8758","Ishaq ibn Ziyad al-Ayli narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Hind ibn Abi Said narrated to us, from Sharik ibn Abi Namir, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Three whose supplication is not rejected: the one who remembers Allah, the supplication of the oppressed, and the just ruler."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Abu Hurayrah through this route, and we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Sharik ibn Abi Namir except Abdullah ibn Said, nor from Abdullah except Humayd ibn al-Aswad."
"8759","Hilal ibn Ali from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah. Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna Abu Musa narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Hilal ibn Ali narrated to us, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The people of Paradise look at one another as the eastern star is seen from the western star on the rising horizon, due to the disparity of degrees."" They said: O Messenger of Allah, who are they? He said: ""People who believed in Allah and affirmed the Messengers."""
"8760","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Hell said: O Lord, permit me two breaths, for I fear I will overflow upon Your creation; so He permitted it two breaths each year, twice: the severity of heat is from its exhalation, and the severity of cold is from its frost."""
"8761","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The son of Adam grows old and his body diminishes, while his heart remains young in love of two things: long life and love of wealth."""
"8762","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Fulayh narrated to us, he said: Hilal ibn Ali narrated to us, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The false oath promotes the goods and erases blessing."""
"8763","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The likeness of the believer is like the tender stalk of crops; from wherever the wind comes, it bends it."""
"8764","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""All my ummah will enter Paradise except whoever refuses."" They said: O Messenger of Allah, and who refuses? He said: ""Whoever obeys me enters Paradise, and whoever disobeys me enters the Fire."""
"8765","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Hilal, meaning Ibn Ali, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever believes in Allah and His Messenger and establishes prayer, it is a right upon Allah to admit him to Paradise, whether he emigrates in the path of Allah or sits where his mother gave birth to him."""
"8766","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: While the Messenger of Allah was one day narrating to his Companions, he said: ""A man from the people of the desert was admitted to Paradise, and he asked his Lord for permission to cultivate, and He said: Are you not in whatever you wish? He said: I wish to increase. He said: So He permitted him, and he sowed, and its growth, ripening, and harvest came in the blink of an eye, and it came like mountains, and it was said: O son of Adam, nothing satisfies you?!"" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from the hadith of Hilal ibn Ali, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah. The hadiths of Hilal ibn Ali from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, we do not know of anyone who narrated them from Ata except Hilal, nor from Hilal except Fulayh; they have been narrated from Abu Hurayrah through other routes. Hilal ibn Ali is a Madani; he is Hilal ibn Usamah, also called Ibn Ali, and he is Ibn Abi Maymunah."
"8767","What Habban ibn Wasi narrated from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah. Safwan ibn al-Mughallis narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Lahiah narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Rabiah narrated to us, from Habban ibn Wasi, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Whoever fasts a day in the path of Allah, Allah distances him from the Fire by seventy autumns."" We do not know of anyone who narrated this hadith from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, except Habban ibn Wasi, and we do not know of Habban ibn Wasi narrating from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, except this hadith."
"8768","What Zayd ibn Aslam narrated from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah. Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah al-Qurashi, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Wife-exchange in the Jahiliyyah was for a man to say to a man: Exchange your wife with me and I will exchange my wife with you; that you give up your wife to me and I give up my wife to you. So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: ""Nor to exchange them for other wives, even though their beauty pleases you."" He said: Uyaynah ibn Hisn al-Fazari entered upon the Prophet, and with him was Aishah, may Allah have mercy on her; he entered without permission, and the Messenger of Allah said to him: ""Where is seeking permission?!"" He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have not sought permission from any man of Mudar since I came of age. Then he said: Who is this little fair one beside you? The Messenger of Allah said: ""This is Aishah, the Mother of the Believers."" He said: Then give her up to me for the best of creation. He said: ""O Uyaynah, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has forbidden that."" He said: When he left, Aishah, may Allah have mercy on her, said: Who is this? He said: ""A foolish man, obeyed, and upon what you see, he is indeed the chief of his people."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated except from Abu Hurayrah with this chain. Ishaq ibn Abdullah narrated it, and Ishaq is very lenient in hadith; we mentioned this hadith only because we did not memorize it from the Messenger of Allah except through this route, so we mentioned it for this defect and clarified the defect in it."
"8769","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Aban ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Jafar al-Madani, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: While a man was praying with his lower garment trailing, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Go and perform wudu."" He came, then he said: ""Go and perform wudu."" So he went and performed wudu, then he came. A man said: O Prophet of Allah, you ordered him to perform wudu, then you said nothing to him. He said: ""He was praying while trailing his lower garment, and Allah, Blessed and Exalted, does not accept the prayer of a man who trails his lower garment."" This hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it with a connected chain except Aban ibn Yazid, nor from Aban except Musa ibn Ismail. Others than those we named narrated it as mawquf. We do not know of Abu Jafar narrating from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, except this hadith; Abu Jafar narrates only from Abu Hurayrah."
"8770","Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd narrated to us, from his father, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not write from me except the Quran; whoever wrote from me other than the Quran, let him erase it. Narrate from the Children of Israel, no harm; whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."" This hadith was narrated by Hammam from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd: the people of knowledge of transmission have agreed upon weakening the reports he narrated. We mentioned his hadith only to show that he contradicted Hammam, and that he is not a proof in what he alone narrates."
"8771","Dawud ibn Farahij, from Abu Hurayrah. Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Attab narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Sulayman ibn Khalaf, known as Ibn Nufayl, narrated to us, he said: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Mufarrij narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Habib ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Khaliq al-Bazzar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Farahij, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: He said, meaning Allah, Blessed and Exalted: ""Fasting is Mine, and I reward for it, and the breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk."""
"8772","He said: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Farahij, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Jibril kept enjoining me regarding the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."" This hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Dawud ibn Farahij, from Abu Hurayrah, except Shubah."
"8773","He said: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Farahij, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept away from his wives, and Shubah said: I think he said: a month. Umar ibn al-Khattab came to him while he was on a mat, and the mat had marked his side, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, Khosrow, he said, I think, and Caesar drink from gold and silver, and you are like this! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""They have had their good things hastened to them in their worldly life."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The month is twenty-nine, like this and like this,"" and he bent the thumb on the third. This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain, and we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Dawud ibn Farahij except Shubah."
"8774","He said: Ruzayq ibn al-Saht narrated to us, he said: Shabab narrated to us, from Shubah. Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Farahij, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: We had no food in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except the two black ones: dates and water. This hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Dawud ibn Farahij, from Abu Hurayrah, except Shubah."
"8775","He said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Athmah narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Yaqub narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Farahij, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""None endures its hardship but I will be an intercessor or witness for him."""
"8776","Al-Abbas ibn al-Faraj said: Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Athmah narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Yaqub narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Dawud ibn Farahij, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Allah, Ibrahim is Your servant and intimate friend; he supplicated You for the people of Makkah, that You bless them in their sa and mudd. I am Your servant and Messenger; I supplicate You for the people of Madinah with what Ibrahim supplicated You for the people of Makkah, that You bless them in their sa and mudd, like what You blessed the people of Makkah in their sa and mudd."" The two hadiths of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq from Dawud ibn Farahij, we do not know of anyone who narrated them from Abd al-Rahman except Musa ibn Yaqub."
"8777","Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Haddadi narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Farahij, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Honor goats and wipe their nasal discharge, for they are among the animals of Paradise."" This hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Dawud, from Abu Hurayrah, except Yazid ibn Abd al-Malik al-Nawfali, and he is not a memorizer, even though a large group narrated from him."
"8778","Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Yazid ibn Abd al-Malik al-Nawfali narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from Dawud ibn Farahij, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There will come upon people a time when one passing by a grave says: I wish I were its occupant instead of its occupant."""
"8779","Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from Dawud ibn Farahij, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah, Blessed and Exalted, keeps accepting repentance from His servant until he rattles in his throat."" We have already mentioned Yazid ibn Abd al-Malik regarding his poor memory, and we have no need to repeat it afterwards."
"8780","Ishaq ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abu Sufyan, the freedman of al-Zubayr, narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Farahij, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on the day of the Conquest sitting, with Abu Bakr standing over his head with a sword. This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayrah except through this route."
"8781","Musa ibn Wardan, from Abu Hurayrah. Yahya ibn Khalaf narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Ata, from Musa ibn Wardan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever dies ill dies a martyr, is protected from the two testers of the grave, and is provided morning and evening with sustenance from Paradise."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Abu Hurayrah with this chain. I think Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Ata is Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Yahya, attributed to his grandfather so as not to be recognized, because Ibrahim ibn Abi Yahya is weak in hadith; the people of knowledge abandoned his hadith."
"8782","Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn al-Rawwas narrated to us, he said: al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, from Musa ibn Wardan, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""In Paradise there are columns of ruby, upon them chambers of emerald, with open doors, shining as the brilliant star shines."" He said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, who dwells in them? He said: ""Those who love one another in Allah, give to one another in Allah, and meet one another in Allah."" This wording, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Abu Hurayrah except Musa ibn Wardan, nor from Musa except Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd. Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd was narrated from by a group of people of knowledge; he was not a memorizer, and he is a well-known Madani."
"8783","What Muhammad ibn Ammar ibn Sad narrated, from Abu Hurayrah. Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us, he said: Abu Nuaym narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Usayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ammar ibn Sad, that he heard Abu Hurayrah mention that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to them that Jibril (peace be upon him) came to him and prayed with him the prayers in two times each, except Maghrib: He came to me and prayed Zuhr when it was like the thong of my sandal, then he came to me and prayed Asr with me when it was like me, then he came to me at Maghrib and prayed with me at the hour the sun set, then he came to me at Isha and prayed with me at the hour of twilight, then he came to me at Fajr and prayed with me at the hour dawn broke, then he came to me the next day and prayed Zuhr with me when the shadow was like me, then he came to me at Asr and prayed with me when it was like me, then he came to me at Maghrib and prayed with me at the hour the sun set, not changing it from its first time, then he came to me at Isha and prayed with me when the first third of the night had gone, then he made it bright for me at Fajr until I saw no star in the sky, then he said: What is between these two is the time. This Muhammad ibn Ammar ibn Sad, we do not know of anyone who narrated from him except Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Usayd."
"8784","Abu Said, the freedman of Abdullah ibn Amir, from Abu Hurayrah. Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us, from Abu Said, the freedman of Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Kurayz, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Do not engage in najsh, do not hate one another, do not turn away from one another, do not envy one another, none of you should sell over another's sale; be servants of Allah, brothers. The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim: he does not wrong him, does not forsake him, does not despise him. Taqwa is here, pointing to his chest. All of the Muslim is forbidden to the Muslim: his blood and his honor. It suffices a man to despise his Muslim brother."" This Abu Said who narrated this hadith from Abu Hurayrah, we do not know of anyone who narrated from him except Dawud ibn Qays. This wording has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah through other than one route."
"8785","Abu al-Saib, the freedman of Hisham. Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Maslamah al-Qanabi narrated to us, from Malik, meaning Ibn Anas, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, that he heard Abu al-Saib, the freedman of Hisham ibn Zuhrah, say: I heard Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever prays a prayer in which he does not recite the Mother of the Quran, it is deficient, incomplete."" I said to him: O Abu Hurayrah, I am sometimes behind the imam. He said: He squeezed my arm and said: Recite it, O Persian, to yourself; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: ""I have divided prayer between Me and My servant into halves; half of it is Mine and half is My servant's, and My servant has what he asks."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, he says: ""Recite."" The servant says: ""All praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds."" Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: My servant has praised Me. He says: ""The Most Merciful, the Most Merciful."" Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: My servant has extolled Me. The servant says: ""Master of the Day of Judgment."" Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: My servant has glorified Me; this verse is between Me and My servant. The servant says: ""You we worship and You we ask for help."" This is between Me and My servant, and My servant has what he asks. The servant says: ""Guide us along the straight path, the path of those You favored, not of those who earned anger, nor of the astray."" These are for My servant, and My servant has what he asks. This wording, we do not know of anyone who narrated it except Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"8786","Ibn Ukaymah, from Abu Hurayrah. Hawtharah ibn Muhammad and Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, they said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn Ukaymah narrating to Said ibn al-Musayyib, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in a prayer we thought was Subh, then he said: ""Has any of you recited behind me?"" A man said: I did. He said: ""I say: Why is the Quran being contended with me?"" So people stopped reciting in what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited aloud in."
"8787","Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us, he said: al-Qanabi narrated to us, from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from Ibn Ukaymah al-Laythi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), adding in it: So people stopped reciting along with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited aloud of the prayers, when they heard that from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This hadith was narrated from al-Zuhri by Malik, Ibn Uyaynah, Mamar, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, and others, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Ukaymah, from Abu Hurayrah. Al-Awzai narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, erring in its chain; al-Zuhri only said: I heard Ibn Ukaymah narrating to Said ibn al-Musayyib, and this is a clear error. The nephew of al-Zuhri narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Ibn Uyaynah and Ibn Ukaymah. We do not know of anyone who narrated from him except al-Zuhri alone."
"8788","Abu al-Hakam al-Laythi, from Abu Hurayrah. Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu al-Hakam al-Laythi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""No prize except in hoof or pad."" We do not know of this Abu al-Hakam narrating from Abu Hurayrah except this hadith."
"8789","What Ubayd ibn Hunayn narrated. Muhammad ibn al-Layth, as far as I know, narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Utbah ibn Muslim, from Ubayd ibn Hunayn, that he informed him that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When a fly falls into one of your drinks, immerse it all, then remove it; in one of its wings is disease, and in the other is cure."" This wording has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah through other than one route, and narrated from Abu Said and from Anas."
"8790","Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us, he said: al-Qanabi informed us, from Malik, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Ubayd ibn Hunayn, the freedman of Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn al-Khattab, informed him that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: I came with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he heard a man reciting: ""Say: He is Allah, One,"" to its end, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It is incumbent."" It was said: What, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""Paradise."" Abu Hurayrah said: I wanted to go to the man to give him glad tidings, then I feared missing lunch with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I preferred lunch; then I returned to the man and found him gone. We do not know of Ubayd ibn Hunayn narrating from Abu Hurayrah except these two hadiths."
"8791","Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah. Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking from the mouth of the waterskin."
"8792","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated it to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""None of you should prevent his neighbor from placing a beam in his wall."""
"8793","Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""When one of you asks his neighbor to place a beam in his wall, let him not prevent him."""
"8794","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn al-Abbas al-Bahili narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Simak, meaning Ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When one of you prays in a garment, let him cross its two ends."" This hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Shubah, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, except Said ibn Amir; it is only known from the hadith of Hisham ibn Abi Abdullah, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah."
"8795","Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Qattan al-Wasiti and Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated to us, they said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""In Paradise there is a palace, I think he said: of pearl, in which there is no crack nor flaw; Allah, Blessed and Exalted, prepared it as hospitality for His intimate friend Ibrahim (peace be upon him)."""
"8796","Ahmad ibn Jamil al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. This hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Hammad ibn Salamah with a connected chain except Yazid ibn Harun and al-Nadr ibn Shumayl; others narrate it as mawquf."
"8797","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man driving a sacrificial camel and said: ""Ride it."" He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: ""Ride it, woe to you,"" or ""woe is you."""
"8798","Al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf, known as Ibn al-Shair, narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he saw a man driving a sacrificial camel and said: ""Ride it."" He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: ""Ride it, woe to you,"" or ""woe is you."""
"8799","Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The cat is among the furnishings of the house."" This hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, except al-Hakam ibn Aban. None narrated it from him except Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam. Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam is not a memorizer; there is softness in his hadith, even though a group narrated from him."
"8800","Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: My intimate friend enjoined upon me three things I do not leave, in travel nor residence: fasting three days of each month, witr before sleep, and the two rakahs of Duha. This hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam except his son. Our mention of him has already come."
"8801","Dawud ibn Sulayman Abu al-Mutarrif narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Umar al-Adani narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""On Friday there is an hour which no servant coincides with, asking Allah for good therein, except He gives it to him."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from the hadith of Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, except from the hadith of al-Hakam ibn Aban. Hafs al-Adani is not trustworthy; he narrated from al-Hakam and others hadiths in which he was not followed."
"8802","Sawwar ibn Sahl al-Dubai narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his family, or some of his family, used to bathe from a single vessel. This hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it except Said ibn Amir, from Hisham; this is its wording, or its meaning."
"8803","Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from Abu Hashim, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, raising it, he said: ""Whoever listens to the speech of people who dislike it, molten lead is poured into his ears."" This hadith has been narrated by more than one as mawquf. More than one narrated it from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas."
"8804","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Hawshab ibn Aqil narrated to us, from Mahdi ibn al-Hajari, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting the day of Arafah at Arafat. This hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, except Mahdi al-Hajari, nor from Mahdi except Hawshab ibn Aqil. Ibn Abbas narrated this hadith; Ikrimah narrated it from him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke fast on the day of Arafah at Arafat."
"8805","Salamah ibn Shabib and Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, they said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, that a Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking help in something; Ikrimah said: I think he said: regarding blood-money. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him something, then said: ""Have I done good to you?"" The Bedouin said: No, nor beautifully. Some of the Muslims became angry and intended to rise against him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) signaled: Hold back. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose and reached his house, he called the Bedouin to the house and said to him: ""You came to us and asked us, and we gave you, and you said what you said."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him more and said: ""Have I done good to you?"" The Bedouin said: Yes; may Allah reward you with good from family and kin. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You came to us and asked us, and we gave you, and you said what you said, and in the hearts of my Companions there is something against you because of that; when you come, say before them what you said before me, so it leaves their chests."" He said: Yes. He said: Al-Hakam narrated to me that Ikrimah said: Abu Hurayrah said: When the Bedouin came, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Your companion came to us and asked us, and we gave him, and he said what he said; we called him and gave him, and he claims he is satisfied. Is that so?"" The Bedouin said: Yes; may Allah reward you with good from family and kin. Abu Hurayrah said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The likeness of me and this Bedouin is like a man who had a she-camel that ran away from him; people followed it and only increased its flight. The owner of the she-camel said to them: Leave me and my she-camel; I am gentler with her and know her better. The owner turned to her, took for her some of the dust of the earth, called her until she came and responded, tied her saddle upon her and mounted her. Had I obeyed you when he said what he said, he would have entered the Fire."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except through this route with this chain."
"8806","Muharrar ibn Abi Hurayrah, from his father. Hawtharah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Mujalid narrated to us, from Amir, from al-Muharrar ibn Abi Hurayrah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""People keep saying: Allah was before everything; what was before Him?"""
"8807","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, he said: Mujalid narrated to us, from Amir al-Shabi, from al-Muharrar ibn Abi Hurayrah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the Dajjal, and he said, I think he said: ""He emerges from the sea of the east."""
"8808","Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from al-Shabi, from al-Muharrar ibn Abi Hurayrah, from his father, he said: I was with Ali when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him to the people of Makkah with Baraah. He said: What would you call out? He said: We would call out: None enters Paradise except a believer, no naked person circumambulates the House, whoever had a covenant between him and the Messenger of Allah, his term or affair is to four months; when the four months pass, Allah is free of the polytheists, and His Messenger; no polytheist performs hajj after this year. I would call out until my voice grew hoarse."
"8809","Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, he said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Qays, meaning Ibn al-Rabi, narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from al-Shabi, from al-Muharrar ibn Abi Hurayrah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. This hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Shaybani except Qays, except a report that reached me from al-Nadr ibn Shumayl, from Shubah, from al-Shaybani. What is preserved is what Ghundar narrated, from Shubah, from al-Mughirah."
"8810","Hanzalah ibn Ali, from Abu Hurayrah. Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Hanzalah ibn Ali, from Abu Hurayrah."
"8811","Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Hanzalah al-Aslami informed me, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the son of Maryam will surely enter ihram at Fajj al-Rawha as a pilgrim or umrah-performer, or he will surely combine both."""
"8812","Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated it to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad, nephew of Juwayriyah, narrated to us, he said: Juwayriyah narrated to us, from Malik, from al-Zuhri, that Hanzalah ibn Ali al-Aslami said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, then he mentioned something similar."
"8813","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qutai narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Ali al-Muqaddami narrated to us, he said: Man ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: I heard Hanzalah ibn Ali, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The grateful eater is like the patient fasting person."""
"8814","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Man ibn Muhammad al-Ghifari narrated to us, he said: I heard Hanzalah ibn Ali narrating from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Every deed of the son of Adam is for him except fasting; it is Mine, and I reward for it. He leaves food and drink for My sake."" These two hadiths, we do not know of anyone who narrated them from Hanzalah except Man ibn Muhammad. Man is a man from the people of Madinah, there is no harm in him."
"8815","Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir. Al-Hasan ibn Qazah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Warith ibn Said narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When one of you is sitting in the sun and it recedes from him, let him move from his seat."""
"8816","Al-Hasan ibn Qazah narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Zayd, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Abu Hurayrah, raising it, he said: ""When you see the crescent, fast, and when you see it, break fast; if it is obscured from you, complete thirty. Your fitr is the day you break fast, your adha is the day you sacrifice; all of Arafah is a standing place, all of Muzdalifah is a standing place, all of Mina is a slaughter place, and all the passes of Makkah are a slaughter place."" Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, we do not know him to have heard from Abu Hurayrah; he heard from Ibn Umar, Jabir, and Anas."
"8817","Al-Sakan ibn Said and Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, they said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best of your kohls is ithmid; it grows hair and clears sight."" This hadith was narrated by Ziyad ibn al-Rabi, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir; I think he erred in it, for had it been preserved from Hisham, from Ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, Hisham from Ibn al-Munkadir from Jabir would have been closer to him than Hisham from Umar ibn Muhammad from his father from Abu Hurayrah. We mentioned that Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir did not hear from Abu Hurayrah, so we withheld mentioning from him except these hadiths, to show that he did not hear from him."
"8818","Abu Ghatfan, from Abu Hurayrah. Musarrif ibn Amr al-Kufi, as far as I know, narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Hamzah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ghatfan al-Murri narrated to me that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""None of you should drink standing; whoever forgets, let him vomit."" This wording has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah through other than one route, with differing wordings; we mentioned each hadith with its wording in its place."
"8819","Muhammad ibn Umar ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Yaqub ibn Utbah, from Abu Ghatfan, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Tasbih is for men, clapping is for women."""
"8820","Abbad ibn Aws, also called Ammar ibn Aws, from Abu Hurayrah. Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: al-Awzai narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, that Abbad ibn Aws informed him, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Every step one of you takes toward prayer, a good deed is written for him thereby, a sin is erased from him thereby, and he is raised a degree thereby."""
"8821","Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: Mubarak ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me that Ammar ibn Aws informed him that he heard Abu Hurayrah narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. We do not know of Abbad ibn Aws nor Ammar narrating except this hadith."
"8822","Abd al-Aziz ibn Marwan from Abu Hurayrah. Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us, he said: Abu Nuaym narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ulayy narrated to us, from his father, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Marwan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The worst in a man is devouring greed and unnerving cowardice."" This wording, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"8823","Abu Abdullah, cousin of Abu Hurayrah. Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Rafi, from Abu Abdullah, cousin of Abu Hurayrah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited ""Not of those who earned anger, nor of the astray,"" he said: Amin, until he made the first row hear."
"8824","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Rafi, from Abu Abdullah, cousin of Abu Hurayrah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them, used to open recitation with ""All praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds."" These two hadiths, we do not know them narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain. Bishr ibn Rafi is not strong, even though a group of people of knowledge narrated from him and narrated from him."
"8825","Jabr ibn Abidah from Abu Hurayrah. Al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Hushaym informed us, he said: Sayyar informed us, from Jabr ibn Abidah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) promised us the campaign of India; if I reach it, I will spend in it my wealth and myself; if I am killed, I am among the best of martyrs, and if I return, I am Abu Hurayrah the freed. This hadith, we do not know it narrated except from Abu Hurayrah, and we do not know for it a chain from Abu Hurayrah except this chain."
"8826","Abu Muzahim, from Abu Hurayrah. Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us. Ibrahim said: Musa narrated to us, he said: Aban, meaning Ibn Yazid, narrated to us. Ibrahim said: Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Harb ibn Shaddad informed us, all of these mentioned from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, he said: Abu Muzahim narrated to me that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever follows a funeral and prays over it, then returns, has a qirat; whoever follows it until its matter is concluded has two qirats."" They said: What are the two qirats? He said: ""The smaller of them is like Uhud."" This Abu Muzahim, we do not know of him narrating except this hadith, though I heard Muhammad ibn Mamar narrating from Harun ibn Ismail al-Khazzaz, from Ali ibn al-Mubarak, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Whoever follows a funeral and prays over it,"" then he mentioned the hadith. I said to Ibn Mamar: It is only narrated, this hadith, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Muzahim. He said: So it is with me. I do not know whether the error is from Ali ibn al-Mubarak, Harun, or Muhammad ibn Mamar."
"8827","Abu Ziyad al-Tahhan from Abu Hurayrah. Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us. Ibrahim ibn Nasr narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us. Ibrahim said: Hafs ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: He saw a man drinking standing and said: ""Would you like a cat to drink with you?"" He said: No. He said: ""One worse than it has drunk with you: the devil."""
"8828","Ibrahim narrated it to us, he said: Amr narrated to us, he said: Shubah informed us, from Abu Ziyad al-Tahhan, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""None of you is saved by his deeds."" They said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah! He said: ""Not even I, unless Allah envelops me with mercy from Him and bounty."" We do not know of Shubah narrating from Abu Ziyad al-Tahhan except these two hadiths."
"8829","What Abd al-Rahman al-Araj narrated from Abu Hurayrah. Salamah ibn Shabib and Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""None of you should prevent his neighbor from placing a beam in his wall."""
"8830","Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated it to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed us, from al-Zuhri, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This hadith has been narrated by a group, from al-Zuhri, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah."
"8831","Ahmad ibn Mansur and Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, they said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, from Yunus, meaning Ibn Yazid, from al-Zuhri, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever attends a funeral and prays over it has a qirat."" This hadith was also narrated by al-Zuhri from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah; it has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah through many routes."
"8832","Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When Friday comes, at every gate of the mosque are angels writing the first, then the first."""
"8833","With its chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""One of you is in prayer as long as he waits for prayer."""
"8834","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Bazi narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best day on which the sun rose is Friday; in it Adam (peace be upon him) was created, and in it the Hour will come."""
"8835","Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. This hadith has been narrated by others than those we mentioned, from al-Zuhri, differing with those we named in its chain."
"8836","Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Saigh narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, raising it, he said: ""My heirs do not divide a dinar nor a dirham; what I leave is charity."" This hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Zuhri, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, except Yunus. Abu al-Zinad narrated it from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"8837","Ismail ibn Masud and Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Bazi narrated to us, they said: Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Adam and Musa argued, peace be upon them. Musa said to Adam: You, whom Allah created with His Hand, breathed into you of His Spirit, and commanded the angels to prostrate to you? Did you expel us, or did you expel your offspring, from Paradise? He said: Adam (peace be upon him) said: You are Musa, whom Allah chose with His messages and His speech, I think he said, and sent down the Torah upon you; do you find that written against me before I was created? He said: Yes. He said: So Adam overcame Musa."" This is the wording of this hadith, or close to it, Allah willing. We do not know of anyone who narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from al-Araj, except Umar ibn Said. Al-Zuhri narrated it from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Salamah, and from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah."
"8838","Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Saigh narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: al-Layth, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated in ""When the sky splits asunder"" and ""Read, in the name of your Lord who created."" This hadith, we do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Araj except Safwan ibn Sulaym. More than one narrated it from Safwan."
"8839","Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: Rabiah ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The strong believer is more beloved to Allah than the weak believer, and in each is good. Be keen on what benefits you, seek help from Allah, and do not be incapable. If something befalls you, do not say: Had it been so and so; say: Allah decreed, and what He willed, He did."" This wording was narrated by Ibn Ajlan from Rabiah, and Ibn Idris narrated it from Rabiah. It is not known to be narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain. Rabiah is a Madani, there is no harm in him."
"8840","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The likeness of the believer is like the tender stalk of crops which the winds bend, and the likeness of the disbeliever is like the firm pine standing on its root, which nothing moves until a wind blows and snaps it."""
"8841","Rizqullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Man ibn Isa narrated to us, from Malik, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer after Asr and after Fajr."
"8842","Harun ibn Musa ibn Abi Alqamah wrote to me, informing me that Abu Damrah Anas ibn Iyad narrated to him, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Water is not withheld to withhold thereby pasture."""
"8843","Harun ibn Musa ibn Abi Alqamah wrote to me, informing me in his letter, from Anas ibn Iyad, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The most beloved lands to Allah, Blessed and Exalted, are mosques, and the most hateful lands to Allah, Blessed and Exalted, are their markets."""
"8844","Amr ibn Abi Amr from al-Araj. Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Amr narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A vow does not bring near anything Allah had not decreed; rather, through a vow is extracted from the miser what he did not intend to give."""
"8845","Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Amr narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Adam and Musa argued. Musa said: O Adam, Allah created you with His Hand, breathed into you of His Spirit, commanded the angels to prostrate to you, then commanded you to dwell in Paradise, eating wherever you wished in abundance, and forbade you one tree, yet you disobeyed your Lord and ate from it. He said: O Musa, did you not know that was decreed for me before He created me? He said: So Adam overcame Musa."""
"8846","8842 - Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Amr narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah; that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man being supported between two men and asked about him; they said: He vowed to perform Hajj on foot, so he said: Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, is Independent of his vow - I think he said: - Order him to ride. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain, and we do not know Amr ibn Abi Amr reported except these hadiths."
"8847","Of the shaykhs from al-Araj 8843 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you withhold - or let none of you refrain - from giving the beggar, even if he sees in his hands two bracelets of gold. And this hadith, we do not know its wording reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this route."
"8848","8844 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril, peace be upon him, advised me and said: When you perform wudu, sprinkle water. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain."
"8849","8845 - And Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you prevent his neighbor from placing a beam in his wall or upon his wall. And this hadith, al-Zuhri and Salih ibn Kaysan have reported it from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah."
"8850","8846 - Amr ibn Bishr al-Naji narrated to us, he said: Mualla ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The owner of the mount is most entitled to its front seat."
"8851","8847 - Amr ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mualla ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most reciting of the Book of Allah among the people leads them in prayer. And these two hadiths, we do not know anyone reported them from al-Hasan ibn Ali, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, except Mualla ibn al-Fadl, and he is a Basran man, there is no harm in him; and this al-Hasan ibn Ali, we do not know anyone reported from him except Abu Qutaybah and Mualla ibn al-Fadl, and all that he reported from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, we do not know anyone shared with him in it except the hadith: Let none of you prevent his neighbor from placing a beam in his wall."
"8852","8848 - Rizq Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Man ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Fadl, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Talbiyah of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: Labbayk, God of truth. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain."
"8853","8849 - Abdah ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Fadl, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn is not stated in this row; the text ends at the attribution to the Prophet.]"
"8854","8850 - And Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated it to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Salih ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Fadl, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed wudu twice, twice. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain."
"8855","8851 - And al-Abbas ibn Abd Allah al-Tarqufi narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Yahya ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Fadl, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Indeed in Paradise there is a tree, a rider travels in its shade for a hundred years."
"8856","8852 - And al-Hasan ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit informed us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Fadl, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from the punishment of Hell, and from the trial of life and death, and from the trial of the False Messiah, the Dajjal."
"8857","8853 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Fadl, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Ibrahim (peace be upon him) was circumcised after eighty years had passed over him, at al-Qadum. And this hadith has been reported from Abu Hurayrah through various routes. And Abd Allah ibn al-Fadl reported from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, sound hadiths known from Abu Hurayrah apart from the report of Abd Allah ibn al-Fadl from al-Araj."
"8858","8854 - Amr ibn Hafs al-Shiyani narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith informed us, from Jafar ibn Rabiah, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Hammah, no Hammah - twice."
"8859","8855 - Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to me, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Jafar, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever is offered perfume should not refuse it, for it is light to carry and sweet in smell. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from Abu Hurayrah with this wording except from this route."
"8860","8856 - Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Bukhari narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Delay the Zuhr prayer in intense heat; for the intensity of heat is from the exhalation of Hell. And this hadith, we do not recall it from the hadith of Salih ibn Kaysan, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, except from the hadith of Sulayman ibn Bilal from him."
"8861","8857 - Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Abu Hafs the poet informed us, he said: My father narrated to me, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the Jews perform Aqiqah for a boy with one ram and do not perform Aqiqah for a girl, or slaughter - the doubt is from him or from his father - so perform Aqiqah, or slaughter, for a boy with two rams, and for a girl with one ram. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, except from this route with this chain."
"8862","8858 - al-Husayn ibn Abi Kabshah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yala narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn al-Subh narrated to us, from Muqatil ibn Hayyan, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, in marfu form, he said: The dowries of the wide-eyed Houris are handfuls of dates and pieces of bread. And this hadith, he only meant: when one gives charity; and this hadith, we do not know it reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except from this route with this chain."
"8863","8859 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A woman is not married together with her paternal aunt nor together with her maternal aunt."
"8864","8860 - And with his chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has ninety-nine names; whoever enumerates them enters Paradise."
"8865","And from the hadith of Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah 8861 - Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you not wonder how Allah diverts from me the abuse of Quraysh and their curse; they abuse Mudhammam and curse Mudhammam, while I am Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And this hadith, we do not know it reported from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain."
"8866","8862 - Ahmad ibn Aban and Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, they said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The most humiliating name before Allah is a man named King of Kings."
"8867","8863 - And Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, as far as I know, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Delaying payment by a rich man is injustice, and if one of you is referred to a solvent man, let him follow it."
"8868","8864 - And with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one's servant has sufficed him the preparation of his food, sparing him its heat and its smoke, let him seat him with him; but if he refuses, let him take a morsel and feed it to him."
"8869","8865 - And with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A vow does not bring to the son of Adam anything that Allah has not decreed for him, but it is thereby extracted from the miser."
"8870","8866 - And with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Surplus water is not withheld so that herbage may thereby be withheld."
"8871","8867 - And with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah, and whoever obeys my commander has obeyed me."
"8872","8868 - And with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You see my Qiblah here, yet neither your humility nor your bowing is hidden from me."
"8873","8869 - And with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: When My servant intends a good deed, write it for him as a good deed; then if he does it, write it as ten like it; and if he intends an evil deed, do not write it; then if he does it, write it as one evil deed."
"8874","8870 - And with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parable of the spender and the miser is like two men wearing a cloak of iron from their breasts to their collarbones; when the spender intends to spend, the armor expands over him until it covers his tracks; and when the miser intends to spend, it contracts behind him, so he tries to stretch it but cannot, he tries to stretch it but cannot."
"8875","8871 - And with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has guaranteed - or Allah has undertaken, and Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has enlisted - for whoever goes out striving in the path of Allah, nothing bringing him out except Jihad and faith in Me and affirmation of My Messenger: if I cause him to die, I admit him to Paradise, and if I return him to the house from which he went out, attaining whatever he attained of reward or booty."
"8876","8872 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, and from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a man looks into his neighbor's house and he throws a pebble at his eye, there is nothing due upon him."
"8877","8873 - Nasr ibn Ali and Zayd ibn Akhzam al-Tai narrated to us; Nasr said: Abd Allah ibn Dawud informed us, and Zayd said: Abd Allah ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud (peace be upon him) said: I shall surely go around tonight to such-and-such women - I think he said a hundred - each woman among them will give birth to a boy who fights in the path of Allah; so he went around them, and none among them became pregnant except one woman; they say: half a human; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had he made the exception, each woman among them would have borne a boy who fights in the path of Allah. And this hadith, we do not know anyone reported it from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, except Abd Allah ibn Dawud."
"8878","8874 - Harun ibn Abi Alqamah wrote to me, informing me in his letter that Abd Allah ibn al-Harith narrated to him, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go out from the gate of al-Shajarah and return by the road of al-Muarras. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from the hadith of Ubayd Allah, from Abu al-Zinad, except from the hadith of Abd Allah ibn al-Harith."
"8879","8875 - al-Hasan ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined the two prayers in Madinah without fear. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from the hadith of Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, except from this route. And we do not know anyone followed Uthman ibn Khalid in this report."
"8880","8876 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabbawayh al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, he said: Shuayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no sanctuary except for Allah and His Messenger. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain."
"8881","8877 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hassan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah, meaning Ibn al-Hasan, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Guard against looking at lepers as you guard against the lion. And this hadith, we do not know anyone reported it, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, except Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Hasan. And we do not know anyone followed him in it."
"8882","8878 - And Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Tariq and Abbad ibn Kathir, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed aid comes from Allah according to the burden, and indeed patience comes from Allah according to the trial. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain."
"8883","8879 - Ammar ibn Khalid al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Ghurab narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding Ramadan: Fast at its sighting and break fast at its sighting; but if it is obscured - meaning over you - then count thirty. And this hadith, we do not know anyone reported it from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, except Ali ibn Ghurab. And some hadith scholars have mentioned that Muhammad ibn Bishr also reported it."
"8884","8880 - Ammar ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Ghurab narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best day on which the sun has risen is Friday; in it there is an hour which no Muslim man meets, asking Allah in it, except he is forgiven. And this hadith, we do not know anyone reported it from Ubayd Allah, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, except Ali ibn Ghurab and Uqbah ibn Khalid."
"8885","8881 - Ammar ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Ghurab narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): That he forbade the sale of uncertainty, and the sale of pebbles."
"8886","8882 - And Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade Shighar, and the sale of uncertainty, and the sale of pebbles."
"8887","8883 - Abd Allah ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Uqbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, and from Ubayd Allah, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayrah; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Euphrates recedes over a mountain of gold, and people fight over it, and ninety-nine out of every hundred are killed. This hadith, we do not know anyone reported it from Ubayd Allah, from Khubayb, from Abu Hurayrah, nor from Ubayd Allah, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, except Uqbah ibn Khalid."
"8888","8884 - Yahya ibn Mualla ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farwi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dream of the believer is a part of forty-five parts of prophethood. And this hadith, we do not know anyone reported it from Ubayd Allah except Abd Allah ibn Umar, and we do not know anyone reported it from Abd Allah except Ishaq ibn Muhammad."
"8889","8885 - Muhammad ibn Harb al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Abu Marwan Yahya ibn Abi Zakariyya al-Ghassani narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels pray for one of you so long as he remains in his prayer place: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him. And this hadith, we do not know anyone reported it from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, except Yahya ibn Abi Zakariyya."
"8890","8886 - And Ishaq ibn Wahb al-Allaf narrated to us, he said: Muhadir ibn al-Muwarri narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer, nor does the thief steal while he is a believer, nor does he drink wine while he drinks it and he is a believer. And this hadith, we do not recall it from the hadith of Hisham ibn Urwah, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, except from the hadith of Muhadir, from Hisham ibn Urwah."
"8891","8887 - Ishaq ibn Ziyad al-Ayli narrated to us, he said: Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the dog laps in the vessel of one of you, let him wash it seven times - I think he said: - one of them with dust. And this hadith, we do not know anyone reported it from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, except Yunus ibn Bukayr."
"8892","8888 - Tahir ibn Khalid ibn Nidhar narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, he said: And Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to me, from Abu al-Zinad, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, I take with You a covenant, for I am only a human; so whichever of the believers I have abused or flogged, make that for him a prayer and purification and a nearness by which he draws near on the Day of Resurrection."
"8893","8889 - And Tahir ibn Khalid ibn Nidhar narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, he said: And Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to me, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until nearly thirty lying Dajjals are sent, each of them claiming he is the Messenger of Allah. And these two hadiths, more than one has reported them, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah; and we do not know anyone reported them, apart from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abu al-Zinad, except Ibrahim ibn Tahman."
"8894","8890 - Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Shuayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The hand of Allah is full-flowing; neither night nor day diminishes it. Abu Bakr said: And Ibn Uyaynah has reported it, from Abu al-Zinad."
"8895","Of what Zayd ibn Aslam reported, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah 8891 - Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Habib al-Raqqi informed us, he said: Ahmad ibn Amr al-Basri al-Bazzar narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sad, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim; he does not betray him, nor lie to him, nor forsake him; everything of the Muslim is inviolable to the Muslim: his honor, his wealth, and his blood; piety is here; it suffices a Muslim man to shun his brother. And this hadith, we do not know anyone reported it except Abu Hurayrah with this chain; and Usamah ibn Zayd reported it from his father, from Ata ibn Yasar; and the correct is Hisham ibn Sad."
"8896","8892 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Khallad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah created Adam, He wiped his back, and every soul He will create until the Day of Resurrection fell from his back; then He assigned a lifespan to each human among them; so Adam (peace be upon him) said: Who are these? - I think he said: - Your sons, he said; and behold, a man among them with light between his eyes; so Adam said: Who is this? He said: This is a man from your progeny in the last of the nations, called Dawud; he said: And how much did You make his lifespan? He said: Sixty years; he said: Then add to it forty years from my lifespan; so when Allah decreed Adam's lifespan, the Angel of Death came to him, and he said: Forty years remain of my lifespan; he said: Did you not give them to your son Dawud? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So he denied, and his progeny denied; and he forgot, and his progeny forgot; and he erred, and his progeny erred."
"8897","8893 - Ibrahim ibn Ziyad and Muhammad ibn Said al-Attar narrated to us, they said: Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile time; for Allah is time. And this hadith, we do not know anyone reported it from Hisham ibn Sad, from Zayd, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, except Abd Allah ibn Numayr."
"8898","8894 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support; your wife says: Spend on me or divorce me, and your child says: To whom do you entrust me, and your slave says: Spend on me or sell me."
"8899","8895 - And Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: al-Muqri narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Ayyub, from Ibn Ajlan, from Zayd, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly, except that he said: O Messenger of Allah, whom do I support? He said: Your wife says: Feed me; your servant says: Feed me and employ me; your child says: To whom do you leave me."
"8900","8896 - al-Abbas ibn Jafar al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mujib narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the people of the highest ranks are seen as you see the brilliant star in the east and the west on the horizon, due to the distance of the ranks; it was said: O Messenger of Allah, are those the Prophets? He said: No, by the One in Whose hand is my soul: people who believed in Allah and His Messenger and affirmed the Messengers."
"8901","8897 - And Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One dirham preceded a hundred thousand dirhams; they said: O Messenger of Allah, how did one dirham precede a hundred thousand dirhams? He said: A man with one dirham gave it in charity, and a man with a hundred thousand dirhams gave them in charity. And this hadith, we do not know it reported except from Abu Hurayrah with this chain. And we do not know anyone reported it from Zayd except Ibn Ajlan."
"8902","8898 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sad al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Imam is appointed only to be followed; so when he says Takbir, say Takbir, and when he bows, bow, and when he recites, listen attentively. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who said in it: And when he recites, listen attentively - except Ibn Ajlan, from Zayd, from Abu Salih; and we do not know anyone reported it from Ibn Ajlan, from Zayd, except Abu Khalid and Muhammad ibn Sad; and al-Layth differed from them."
"8903","8899 - And Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, he said: al-Qaqa narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam and Ubayd Allah ibn Miqsam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No contagion, no Hammah, no Ghul, no Safar. And we do not know anyone combined these, from Abu Salih, except Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Ibn Ajlan."
"8904","8900 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whatever I tell you is from Allah, it is that about which there is no doubt. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from Abu Hurayrah except from this route with this chain."
"8905","8901 - And Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, from al-Layth, from Ibn Ajlan, from Zayd ibn Aslam and al-Qaqa ibn Hakim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Religion is sincere advice. And this hadith, Hisham ibn Sad reported it, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar."
"8906","8902 - Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Abu Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A man removed a thorny branch from the road - or he cut a tree - or it was - I think he said: - harm, so he cleared it away; so Allah thanked him and admitted him to Paradise."
"8907","8903 - Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): That a man never did any good at all, and he used to lend to people; he used to say to his agent: Take what is easy and leave what is difficult, and overlook, that Allah may overlook us. So when he died, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: Did you ever do any good for Me? He said: No, except that I had an agent, and I used to say: Overlook, that Allah may overlook us. He said: Then I have overlooked you."
"8908","8904 - Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from Abu Salih and Ata ibn Yasar and Busr ibn Said and Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever catches a rakah of Fajr before the sun rises has not missed it, and whoever catches a rakah of Asr before the sun sets has not missed it."
"8909","8905 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Rawh narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih and Ata ibn Yasar - I think he said: - and Busr ibn Said, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"8910","8906 - And Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mundhir Ismail ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever grants respite to one in hardship or remits for him, Allah shades him under the shade of His Throne on a day when there is no shade except His shade. And this hadith, we do not know anyone reported it from Zayd, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, except Dawud ibn Qays; and some companions of Dawud reported it from Dawud, from Zayd; he said: And I do not know it except from Abu Salih."
"8911","8907 - Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Layth ibn Sad, from Hisham ibn Sad, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever fasts a day in the path of Allah, Allah distances him from the Fire by seventy autumns."
"8912","8908 - And Khalifah ibn Hawdhah ibn Khalifah narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us. 8909 - And Ahmad ibn Abd Allah al-Sadusi and Ali ibn Ishkab narrated to us, they said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Zuhayr, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am as My servant thinks of Me, and I am with him when he remembers Me."
"8913","8910 - And Ali ibn Ashkib narrated to us, he said: Rawh narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, is more joyful at the repentance of His servant - I think he said: - than one of you finding his lost animal in the desert."
"8914","8910 / 2 - And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the servant draws near to Allah, Blessed and Exalted, by a span, Allah draws near to him by a cubit; and when he draws near by a cubit, Allah draws near to him by a fathom; and when he comes to Me walking, I come to him hastening."
"8915","8911 - Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qutai narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Suhban narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I make half my prayer supplication for you? He said: As you wish. He said: Then shall I make two-thirds of my prayer supplication for you? He said: Yes. He said: Then shall I make all my prayer supplication for you? He said: Then Allah will suffice you the concern of this world and the Hereafter. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain; and we do not know anyone narrated it from Zayd except Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Suhban, and he was not a memorizer."
"8916","8912 - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah al-Sadusi narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Horses are of three kinds: for a man a reward, for a man a covering, and upon a man a burden; as for that which is a reward for him: a man who ties it in the path of Allah and lengthens its tether in a meadow or garden, so whatever it grazes within that tether of the meadow or garden is good deeds for him; and if it breaks that tether and runs a hill or two, its urine and dung are good deeds for him; and if it passes a river and drinks from it, that is good deeds for him, so it is a reward for him. And a man who ties it for self-sufficiency and does not forget the right of Allah regarding its backs, so it is a covering for that. And a man who ties it for pride and show and enmity toward the people of Islam, so it is a burden for that. And Suhayl has reported it, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah."
"8917","8913 - Abd Allah ibn Shabib narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The two eyes commit adultery, and the tongue commits adultery, and the private part confirms that or denies it."
"8918","8914 - And with it, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The first who let loose the Saibah and set up the idols and changed the covenant of my father Ibrahim (peace be upon him) was Amr ibn Luhayy; I have seen him in the Fire dragging his intestines."
"8919","Of what Abu Hazim reported from Abu Salih 8915 - Ismail ibn Masud al-Jahdari narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abu Hazim narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in the pledge: In your energy and your dislike, and preference over you. And this hadith, we do not know anyone reported it from Abu Hazim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, except Fudayl ibn Sulayman."
"8920","8916 - And with it, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: When Allah loves a servant, He calls Jibril - I think he said: - Indeed Allah has loved so-and-so, so love him. And this hadith, more than one has reported it from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, in marfu form."
"8921","8917 - Ishaq ibn Wahb al-Allaf narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I abused a man in Islam through his mother in Jahiliyyah, so he complained against me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed in you is a branch of disbelief. So when he mentioned disbelief, my legs trembled, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, by the One who sent you with the truth, I shall never abuse a Muslim after it, ever. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from Abu Hurayrah except from this route with this chain."
"8922","8918 - Harun ibn Musa al-Farwi wrote to me, informing that his father narrated to him, from Hisham ibn Sad, from Zayd ibn Aslam and Abu Hazim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah; and Zayd and Abu Hazim, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever catches a rakah of the Asr prayer before the sun sets has not missed the prayer, and whoever catches a rakah of Fajr before the sun rises has not missed the prayer."
"8923","8918 (m) - Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever guards what is between his jaws and between his legs enters Paradise. And this hadith, Abu Khalid reported it from Ibn Ajlan, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah; and al-Muqaddami reported it, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sad."
"8924","8919 - Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Abu Sakhr, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The believer is affectionate, and there is no good in one who is not affectionate nor is shown affection. Thus Abu Sakhr said, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah; and Musab ibn Thabit reported it from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sad. Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah."
"8925","8920 - Abdah ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib, meaning Ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the slave-girl of one of you commits adultery, let him flog her; then if she commits adultery, let him flog her; then if she commits adultery, let him sell her even for a rope. And this hadith, we do not know anyone reported it from Sufyan, from Habib, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, except Muawiyah ibn Hisham."
"8926","8921 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Sinan Said ibn Sinan narrated to us, he said: Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah; that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, a man does a deed concealing it, then when it is discovered he is pleased; he said: For him is the reward of secrecy and the reward of openness."
"8927","8922 - And Muhammad ibn Abi Ghalib narrated to us, he said: Abu Salih al-Farra narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Hamzah al-Zayyat, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) demanding payment, having lent him half a wasq, so he gave him a wasq. He said: Half a wasq is yours, and half is yours from me. Then the owner of the wasq came demanding it, so he gave him two wasqs, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A wasq is yours, and a wasq is yours from me. And this hadith, we do not know anyone reported it from Habib, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, except Hamzah al-Zayyat, nor from Hamzah except Ibn al-Mubarak."
"8928","8923 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Habib, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah, and whoever obeys my commander has obeyed me, and whoever disobeys the commander has disobeyed me."
"8929","Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah 8924 - Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan and al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, they said: Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Imam is a guarantor, and the muezzin is trusted; O Allah, guide the Imams and forgive the muezzins. And this hadith is known only from the hadith of al-Amash; and I do not think Abu Ishaq heard it from Abu Salih; and he has reported another hadith from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah."
"8930","Abu al-Zubayr, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah 8925 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Soon the livers of mounts will be beaten, and no scholar more knowledgeable than the scholar of Madinah will be found. And we do not know Abu al-Zubayr reported from Abu Salih except this hadith. And none reported it from Ibn Jurayj except Ibn Uyaynah."
"8931","Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari 8926 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that I would burden my Ummah, I would not stay behind a detachment going out; but I do not find what to carry them upon, nor do they find what to bear themselves with, and it burdens them to stay behind me; and I would love to be killed in the path of Allah, then brought to life, then killed, then brought to life."
"8932","8927 - Abu Mahdhurah al-Warraq narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Masud narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere, except al-Masjid al-Haram. And thus al-Harith ibn Umayr reported it from Yahya ibn Said, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah; and others reported it from Yahya ibn Said, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah."
"8933","al-Qaqa ibn Hakim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah 8928 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: May Allah have mercy on a man who rises at night and prays and wakes his wife, so she prays; but if she acts, otherwise he sprinkles water on her face; may Allah have mercy on a woman who rises at night and prays and wakes her husband, so he prays; but if he acts, otherwise she sprinkles water on his face."
"8934","8929 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Qays narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, he said: I heard him mention it from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a fly falls in the vessel of one of you, let him dip it, then take it out; for in one of its wings is disease and in the other is cure, and it begins with the disease, so dip it, then take it out. And this hadith, we do not know anyone reported it from Ibn Ajlan, from al-Qaqa, except Muhammad ibn Qays; and he has been contradicted in it from Ibn Ajlan."
"8935","8930 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said and Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, they said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am to you only like a father, teaching you: when one of you comes to the privy, let him not face the Qiblah nor turn his back to it; and when one of you cleans himself, let him not clean himself with his right hand; and he used to command three stones. And he forbade dung and decayed bones. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from Abu Hurayrah except from this route."
"8936","8931 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from al-Qaqa, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man supplicating thus with his finger, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Thus, One, One."
"8937","8932 - And Amr narrated to us, he said: Safwan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from al-Qaqa, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The martyr feels no pain except as one of you feels a pinch."
"8938","8933 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Safwan narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from al-Qaqa, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is none who goes out in the path of Allah - and Allah knows best who goes out in His path - except he comes on the Day of Resurrection with his wound flowing blood; the color is the color of blood and the smell is the smell of musk."
"8939","8934 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Safwan narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from al-Qaqa ibn al-Hakim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the believer sins, there is a black spot in his heart; then if he repents and desists and seeks forgiveness, it is polished; but if he returns, it increases until the heart blackens; that is the covering which Allah, Blessed and Exalted, mentioned: {Nay, but covering is upon their hearts what they earned}."
"8940","8935 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Safwan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from al-Qaqa, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Religion is sincere advice; they said: For whom, O Messenger of Allah? He said: For Allah, and for His Book, and for the leaders of the Muslims, and for their common folk."
"8941","8936 - Yusuf ibn Salman narrated to us, he said: Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, and from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The adulterer does not commit adultery while he commits it and he is a believer, nor does he steal while he steals and he is a believer, nor does he drink wine while he drinks it and he is a believer. And this hadith, we do not know anyone reported it from Ibn Ajlan, from al-Qaqa, from Abu Salih, and from Abu al-Zinad, except Hatim."
"8942","8937 - Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed part of the perfection of faith is good character."
"8943","8938 - Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Yazid informed us, he said: Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to me, from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There remains over this affair - or upon this affair - a group from my Ummah; the opposition of whoever opposes them does not harm them, until the command of Allah comes to them."
"8944","8939 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Janah narrated to us, he said: Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from al-Qaqa, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not withhold milk in camels and sheep; so whoever sells them with milk withheld, the buyer has the choice: if he wishes, he takes, and if he wishes, he returns it with a sa of dates. And this hadith, we heard it only from Muhammad ibn Miskin, from Ibrahim ibn Janah, from Hatim, from Ibn Ajlan, from al-Qaqa. And it has been reported from Abu Hurayrah through other routes."
"8945","8940 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The heart of the old man is young in love of two things: in long life, and in abundant wealth. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from the hadith of al-Qaqa except through the report of al-Layth."
"8946","8941 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from al-Qaqa, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. And the believer is one whom people trust with their wealth and their blood. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from Abu Hurayrah except from this route."
"8947","8942 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The treasure of one of you will be on the Day of Resurrection a bald serpent that keeps following him - I think he said: - then it bites his finger, or a word like it."
"8948","8943 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from al-Qaqa, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Upon every soul of the children of Adam is written its share of adultery, which it will surely attain: the eye, its adultery is looking; the ear, its adultery is listening; the hand, its adultery is seizing; the foot, its adultery is walking; the tongue, its adultery is speech; and the heart inclines and wishes; and the private part confirms that or denies it."
"8949","8944 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Adam met Musa, and Musa said to him a word that escaped Abu Bakr al-Bazzar; then Adam said to him: And are you Musa to whom Allah gave the Torah? He said: Yes. He said: Then in how long before my creation do you find the Torah was written? Musa said: Such-and-such. Adam said: Then did you not find in it my sin? He said: Yes. He said: Then do you blame me for something Allah wrote upon me before my creation? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So Adam overcame Musa in argument."
"8950","8945 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from al-Qaqa, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Wealth is not from abundance of goods, but wealth is wealth of the soul."
"8951","8946 - And Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to me, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to me, from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim and Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah; that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man came to a well to drink from it, and upon the well was a dog; so he removed one of his shoes and scooped for it and gave it drink; so Allah thanked him and admitted him to Paradise."
"8952","8947 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And he was asked about the lost sheep? He said: It is for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf. And he was asked about the lost camel? He said: What have you to do with it; with it are its water-skin, or its water-skin and its shoes; leave it until its owner finds it. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from the hadith of al-Qaqa except from the hadith of Yahya ibn Ayyub."
"8953","8948 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from al-Qaqa, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah; and Zayd ibn Aslam and Ubayd Allah ibn Miqsam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No contagion, no Ghul, no Hammah, no Safar."
"8954","8949 - And Muhammad ibn Rizq Allah al-Kalwadhi narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from al-Qaqa, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I was only sent to perfect noble morals."
"8955","Of Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah; Ibn Ajlan from Sumayy 8950 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah; that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he sneezed, placed his hand or his garment upon his face and lowered, or softened with it, his voice. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from Abu Hurayrah except from this route with this chain."
"8956","8951 - Jamil ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah; that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded spreading the arms in prayer, so people complained to him of weakness, so he commanded them to seek help with the knees."
"8957","8952 - And Ahmad ibn Mansur and Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated it to us, and I found that written with me from them, he said: Muadh ibn Faddalah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from Abu Hurayrah except from this route."
"8958","8953 - And Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The poor came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The report breaks off here; the rest of the complaint is in the following row.]"
"8959","8954 - And Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ibn Ajlan, from Sumayy and Raja, meaning Ibn Haywah, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The poor complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, the rich have taken the highest ranks and lasting bliss; they pray as we pray and fast as we fast, and apart from that they have wealth from which they give charity and free slaves; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not tell you of something by which you catch those who preceded you and none after you catches you except one who does like what you did? They said: Yes. He said: You glorify Allah after every prayer ten times, and magnify ten times, and praise fifteen times. And we do not know anything reported from Raja ibn Haywah, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, except this hadith."
"8960","8955 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says morning and evening: Glory be to Allah and with His praise, none comes on the Day of Resurrection with better than what he brought. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this route with this chain."
"8961","8956 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The accepted Hajj has no reward except Paradise, and Umrah to Umrah expiates what is between them. And this hadith, more than one has reported it from Sumayy; and the highest who reported it from Sumayy is Suhayl; and we do not know Suhayl reported from Sumayy except three hadiths: these two and a hadith."
"8962","8957 - Ahmad ibn al-Hajjaj ibn al-Salt narrated it to us, he said: My uncle Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated to me, he said: Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Suhayl, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever sleeps with grease on his hand and something befalls him, let him blame none but himself. And this hadith, Ibrahim ibn Tahman reported it from Suhayl, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah."
"8963","Of Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah from Sumayy 8958 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The nearest a servant is to Allah is while prostrating. And this hadith, we do not know anyone reported it from Sumayy except Umarah; and we do not know it reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this route."
"8964","Of al-Thawri from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah 8959 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Umrah expiates what is between it and the next Umrah, and the accepted Hajj has no reward except Paradise. And we do not know al-Thawri reported from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, except this hadith."
"8965","Of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar from Sumayy, from Abu Salih 8960 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-Sanani narrated to us, he said: al-Mutamir narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The poor came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: The rich have taken the highest ranks and lasting bliss; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And what is that? They said: They pray as we pray, and fast as we fast, and they have wealth from which they give charity and free slaves, and we do not find. He said: Shall I not guide you to a matter which, if you do it, none before you precedes you and none after you catches you except one who does like what you did: Glory be to Allah thirty-three times after every prayer, and praise thirty-three, and magnify thirty-four. So they did; then that reached the rich, so they did what the poor said; then they returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we did what you commanded us, and they do what we do. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is the bounty of Allah, He gives it to whom He wills. And this hadith, we do not know anyone reported it from Ubayd Allah, from Sumayy, except al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman."
"8966","Of Malik ibn Anas from Sumayy 8961 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Travel is a portion of torment; it deprives one of you of his drink and his sleep; so when one of you finishes his need, let him hasten to his family."
"8967","8962 - And Amr narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If people knew what is in the call to prayer and the first row and found no way except to draw lots for it, they would draw lots for it; and if they knew what is in early going, they would race to it; and if they knew what is in Isha and Fajr, they would come to them even crawling."
"8968","8963 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Umrah expiates what is between it and the next Umrah, and the accepted Hajj has no reward except Paradise."
"8969","8964 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Masadah narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: Glory be to Allah and with His praise, Allah removes his sins, even if they are more than the foam of the sea."
"8970","8965 - And Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Malik ibn Anas, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The martyrs are five: the plague-stricken, the one with abdominal illness, the crushed, the drowned, and the woman in childbed."
"8971","8966 - Muhammad ibn Umar al-Muqaddami narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farwi narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr."
"8972","8967 - Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever releases a regretful buyer, Allah releases his slip on the Day of Resurrection. And these two hadiths which al-Farwi reported from Malik, we do not know anyone shared with him in them."
"8973","8968 - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah; that a man passed a thorny branch and moved it from the road, so Allah admitted him to Paradise."
"8974","8969 - And with his chain, that a man - or a woman - passed a dog eating dust from thirst, so the man or the woman took the shoe and began scooping water for it, or gave it drink, so Allah admitted him to Paradise - or admitted her to Paradise."
"8975","8970 - And with his chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Imam says: Allah hears whoever praises Him, then say: Our Lord, to You is praise."
"8976","Of Ibn Uyaynah from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah 8971 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed us, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge from the severity of misery, and the evil of decree, and the gloating of enemies. And this hadith, we do not know anyone reported it from Sumayy except Ibn Uyaynah."
"8977","8972 - And Abd al-Ala ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat, and whoever waits for it until it is buried has two qirats. And this hadith, none reported it from Sumayy except Ibn Uyaynah."
"8978","8973 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Umrah expiates what is between it and the next Umrah, and the accepted Hajj has no reward except Paradise. Of Abd Allah ibn Dinar, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah."
"8979","8974 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Faith is sixty-odd, or seventy-odd branches; the best of them is the testimony that there is no god but Allah, and the lowest of them is removing harm from the road; and modesty is a branch of faith."
"8980","8975 - And Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated it to us, he said: Abu Khalid narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"8981","8976 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Dinar narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Indeed when Allah loves a servant - I think he said: - He calls Jibril - I think he said: - in the heaven: Indeed Allah has loved so-and-so, so love him; then acceptance is placed for him on earth."
"8982","8977 - And Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you sneezes, let him say: Praise be to Allah; and let his brother, or his companion, say to him: May Allah have mercy on you; and let him say: May Allah guide you and set right your state. And this hadith, we do not know it reported from Abu Hurayrah except from this route; and we do not know a more authentic report from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding: May Allah guide you and set right your state, than this hadith."
"8983","8978 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Dinar narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever is given wealth by Allah and does not pay its Zakat, there is made for him on the Day of Resurrection a bald serpent with two spots; it seizes his jaws on the Day of Resurrection, then says: I am your treasure; then he recited this verse {And let not those who are miserly} to the end of the verse."
"8984","8979 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Dinar narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Indeed a servant speaks a word pleasing to Allah, paying it no attention, and Allah raises him by it degrees; and indeed a servant speaks a word angering Allah, paying it no attention, and he falls by it into Hell."
"8985","8980 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Dinar, from his father, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever gives in charity the equivalent of a date from lawful earning - and nothing ascends to Allah, Blessed and Exalted, except what is lawful - then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, accepts it with His right hand, then nurtures it as one of you nurtures his foal, until it becomes like the mountain."
"8986","8981 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah loves a servant, He calls Jibril: Indeed Allah has loved so-and-so, so love him; so Jibril loves him; then he calls among the people of heaven: Indeed Allah has loved so-and-so, so love him; so the people of heaven love him; then acceptance is placed for him on earth."
"8987","8982 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, as I think, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Dinar narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah. [The matn is not stated in this row; the chain ends at Abu Hurayrah.]"
"8988","8983 - And I heard my father narrating it, from Amr ibn Marzuq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah, from his father, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Wretched is the servant of the dinar and the servant of the dirham; wretched and cast down; and if pricked by a thorn, may he not find relief; and blessed is a servant who holds the reins of his horse: if he is in guard duty, he is in guard duty. [The source text ends abruptly here.]"
"8989","8984 - Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The womb is a branch; whoever joins it, Allah joins him; and whoever cuts it, He cuts him - or Allah cuts him."
"8990","8985 - Abdah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Dinar, he said: I heard my father mention, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A man passed a thorny branch and moved it from the road; so Allah thanked him and admitted him to Paradise."
"8991","8986 - Abda narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad informed us from Abd al-Rahman, he said: I heard my father, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah: that a man saw a dog eating dust out of thirst, so the man took his khuff (leather sock) and began to scoop water for it until he quenched it, so Allah thanked him and admitted him to Paradise."
"8992","'Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu Salih. 8987 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Sufyan, meaning Ibn Uyaynah, narrated to us from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Three whom Allah will not speak to on the Day of Resurrection: a man who swore over merchandise that he was offered for it more than he was offered, and a man who withheld surplus water, so Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: Today I withhold My bounty from you just as you withheld the surplus of what your hands did not produce. And a man who swore an oath after the 'Asr prayer to cut off thereby the wealth of a Muslim man. 8988 - Ahmad ibn Mansur said, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yunus, and he once said: Sufyan, from 'Amr, from Abu Salih, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did not mention Abu Hurairah; and he said: He narrated to us with it once, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, and he did not mention the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"8993","Al-Khasib ibn Jahdar, from Abu Salih. 8989 - Talut ibn 'Abbad narrated to us, he said: Al-Rabi' ibn Muslim narrated to us from Khusayb ibn Jahdar, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah: that a man complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of poor memorization, so he said: Seek help with your right hand for your memorization. And this hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this angle with this chain. And al-Khusayb ibn Jahdar is a man from the people of Basra; al-Rabi' ibn Muslim and 'Anbasah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated from him."
"8994","8990 - 'Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: 'Anbasah narrated to us from Khusayb ibn Jahdar, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate with a leper and said: Out of faith in Allah and reliance upon Him. And this hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Abu Hurairah except from this angle with this chain."
"8995","8991 - Al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Uruzzi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Harun ibn Abi 'Isa narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, that Abu Salih al-Samman narrated to him, from Abu Hurairah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying to Aktham ibn al-Jawn: O Aktham, I saw 'Amr ibn Luhayy ibn Qam'ah dragging his entrails in the Fire, and I never saw a man resembling a man more than his resemblance to you. Aktham said: O Messenger of Allah, will his resemblance harm me? He said: No; he is a disbeliever. He was the first to change the religion of Isma'il, so he let loose the sa'ibah, and made the bahirah, and joined the wasilah, and protected the hami. And this hadith, we do not know it to be narrated with this wording except with this chain. And something similar to it has been narrated with other than its wording from Abu Hurairah, and we do not know Muhammad ibn Ibrahim to have narrated with a chain from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, except this hadith."
"8996","Duwayd ibn Nafi', from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah. 8992 - Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Hanan al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Dubarah ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Sulayk narrated to us from Duwayd ibn Nafi', he said: Abu Salih al-Samman narrated to us, he said: Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from dissension, hypocrisy, and evil character. And this hadith, we do not know it to be narrated except from Abu Hurairah with this chain."
"8997","Abd al-'Aziz ibn Rufay', from Abu Salih. 8993 - Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn 'Amr narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Musa ibn Abd Allah ibn Talhah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-'Aziz ibn Rufay' narrated to me from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have left among you two things; you will never go astray after them ever: the Book of Allah and my Sunnah, and they will never separate until they come to me at the Hawd (Pool)."
"8998","8994 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn 'Amr narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Musa narrated to us from Abd al-'Aziz ibn Rufay', from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man being killed while held captive (sabran) is an expiation for his previous sins. And the two hadiths of Salih ibn Musa from Abd al-'Aziz from Abu Salih, we do not know them to be narrated from Abu Hurairah except from this angle with this chain, and Salih ibn Musa is weak (layyin) in hadith."
"8999","8995 - Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Hanan narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from Abd al-'Aziz ibn Rufay', from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah. (The matn is suspended here; its completion follows in the next narration.)"
"9000","8996 - And al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah narrated it to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Abd al-'Aziz ibn Rufay', from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, he said: Two Eids coincided in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a single day; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two Eids have coincided on this day of yours, so whoever of you wishes, it suffices him instead of the Friday prayer, but we will hold the congregation, Allah willing. And the hadith of al-Mughirah from Abd al-'Aziz, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Shu'bah with a connected chain except Baqiyyah; and the hadith of Abd al-'Aziz ibn Rufay' from Abu Salih from Abu Hurairah has been narrated by more than one from Abu Salih as mursal."
